-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 1ב', §1.25 חופשות והיעדרויות
-- Vacations and absences: the holiday and summer vacations and their pay,
-- May Day, sick leave and the days charged to it, compensation for unused
-- sick leave, marriage leave, pregnancy, birth and adoption, paid and unpaid
-- leave, absences for studies and examinations, reserve duty, national
-- sport representation, testimony, Memorial Day, the value deducted for an
-- hour of absence, and principal-selection committees.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `1.25 חופשות והיעדרויות`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25/p2 Navigation line of the source page ("the contents on this page").
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25/p3 Table-of-contents line naming sub-section 1.25.1.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25/p4 Table-of-contents line naming sub-section 1.25.2.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25/p5 Table-of-contents line naming sub-section 1.25.3.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25/p6 Navigation line of the source page ("more contents on the subject").

-- Actors the takanon's shared Party list does not hold. Declared here, and
-- used only by the rules that need them.
@desc Bodies section 1.25 gives powers or duties to that the takanon's shared party list does not name.
DECLARE `1.25 party` IS ONE OF
    `the teaching-manpower division`  @desc אגף כוח אדם בהוראה, the Ministry's division (or its district departments) that decides on leave
    `the paid-leave committee`        @desc הוועדה לחופשות בשכר at the Ministry's head office
    `a district committee`            @desc a district committee chaired by the district manager
    `the sick-days fund`              @desc קרן ימי מחלה לעובדי הוראה
    `the study fund`                  @desc the study fund (קרן השתלמות) a sabbatical is taken from

-- Dates are numbers YYYYMMDD (1 September 1993 is 19930901). Periods are in
-- days unless a name says otherwise.

§§ `1.25.1 חופשות החגים — כללי`

DECLARE `vacation action` IS ONE OF
    `publish the vacation calendar`
    `be absent on a school day`
    `request a permit to be absent`
    `hold a May Day celebration, procession or flag-raising`
    `notify the principal in writing of a May Day absence`
    `organise the school day around the absences`
    `notify the parents that a class cannot be occupied`
    `be at the institution as usual`
    `notify the supervisor of a May Day absence`
    `pay the holiday vacation` HAS `holiday pay paid` IS A NUMBER
    `exchange a fixed inspectors' leave day for another day`

-- §1.25.1 general 1: the Ministry publishes the vacation calendar every year
-- in the Director-General's circulars, by stratum and type of institution.
-- Time in months of the year.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_1__para_1
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `vacation action`
DECIDE `publishing the vacation calendar` IS
    PARTY `the Ministry of Education`
    MUST  `publish the vacation calendar`
    WITHIN 12
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Ministry of Education` BECAUSE "section 1.25.1 general 1: the vacation calendar is published every year"

-- §1.25.1 general 2: on every day the calendar does not list, the full timetable is held.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_1__para_2
GIVEN `the day is in the vacation calendar` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the full timetable is held` `the day is in the vacation calendar` IF
    NOT `the day is in the vacation calendar`

-- §1.25.1 general 3: teaching employees must be at their institutions on every
-- school day; in exceptional cases they may ask the district manager, with
-- reasons, for a permit to be absent; no one is absent before the permit.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_1__para_3
GIVEN `a permit was granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `vacation action`
DECIDE `presence on school days` `a permit was granted` IS
    IF `a permit was granted`
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MAY   `be absent on a school day`
    ELSE    (PARTY `the teaching employee`
             SHANT `be absent on a school day`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.1 general 3: no absence on a school day before the district manager's permit")
         ROR
            (PARTY `the teaching employee`
             MAY   `request a permit to be absent`)

-- §1.25.1 general 4 and §1.25.3.1(11)(a), the same rule twice: illness in the
-- summer, Sukkot, Hanukkah or Passover vacation, with a medical certificate,
-- is not charged to the sick-leave quota.
DECLARE `kind of vacation` IS ONE OF
    `the summer vacation`
    `the Sukkot vacation`
    `the Hanukkah vacation`
    `the Passover vacation`
    `another vacation`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_1__para_4 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p98
GIVEN v IS A `kind of vacation`, `brought a medical certificate` IS A BOOLEAN, `days ill in the vacation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick days charged for illness in a vacation` v `brought a medical certificate` `days ill in the vacation` IS
    IF `brought a medical certificate` AND NOT v EQUALS `another vacation`
    THEN 0
    ELSE `days ill in the vacation`

-- §1.25.1 general 5: an employee of the official institutions who works in a
-- holiday vacation with the Ministry's approval is paid in addition. The
-- amount is set elsewhere; it is an input.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_1__para_5
GIVEN `employed in an official institution` IS A BOOLEAN, `worked in the holiday vacation with the Ministry's approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `the additional payment for that work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `additional payment for work in a holiday vacation` `employed in an official institution` `worked in the holiday vacation with the Ministry's approval` `the additional payment for that work` IS
    IF `employed in an official institution` AND `worked in the holiday vacation with the Ministry's approval`
    THEN `the additional payment for that work`
    ELSE 0

§§ `1.25.1 חופשות החגים — זכאות`

DECLARE `staff status` IS ONE OF
    `on the permanent staff`
    `a substitute`

-- §1.25.1 entitlement 1, second paragraph: these count as days of work.
DECLARE `kind of day before the holiday` IS ONE OF
    `a day of work`
    `paid sick leave`
    `reserve duty`
    `maternity leave paid by national insurance`
    `a study day charged to a training grant`
    `mourning leave`
    `unpaid leave`
    `another absence`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_1/p2
GIVEN k IS A `kind of day before the holiday`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `counts as a day of work for the holiday` k IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `unpaid leave` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `another absence` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@desc A teaching employee facing one holiday vacation, as section 1.25.1's entitlement paragraphs ask about it.
DECLARE `holiday case` HAS
    `status for the holiday`                       IS A `staff status`
    `last day before the holiday`                  IS A `kind of day before the holiday`
    `on unpaid leave after the holiday`            IS A BOOLEAN @desc includes additional leave after a birth
    `the unpaid leave before was approved by the Ministry` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days of substitution`                         IS A NUMBER
    `workdays before the vacation`                 IS A NUMBER
    `days of the holiday vacation`                 IS A NUMBER
    `returned to work the day after the vacation`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `months worked before the vacation`            IS A NUMBER
    `work ended with the end of studies before the holiday` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the returning permanent employee is entitled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the permanent employee the substitute replaced, returning, is entitled to holiday pay

-- §1.25.1 entitlement 1: a member of the permanent staff who worked before the
-- holiday is paid for it, whatever the total of days worked; the note: one on
-- unpaid leave before and/or after the holiday is not.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_1/p3
GIVEN h IS A `holiday case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the permanent staff rule pays the holiday` h IF
        h's `status for the holiday` EQUALS `on the permanent staff`
    AND `counts as a day of work for the holiday` (h's `last day before the holiday`)
    AND NOT h's `on unpaid leave after the holiday`

-- §1.25.1 entitlement 2, "notwithstanding general 3 and entitlement 1": unpaid
-- leave taken before the holiday WITH the Ministry's approval does not cost
-- the holiday; leave without its consent costs the salary, and the employee
-- is treated as one who stopped work without leave (return needs approval).
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_2
GIVEN h IS A `holiday case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `approved unpaid leave before the holiday keeps the holiday pay` h IF
        h's `status for the holiday` EQUALS `on the permanent staff`
    AND h's `last day before the holiday` EQUALS `unpaid leave`
    AND h's `the unpaid leave before was approved by the Ministry`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_2/p2
GIVEN h IS A `holiday case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `left without the Ministry's consent` h IF
        h's `last day before the holiday` EQUALS `unpaid leave`
    AND NOT h's `the unpaid leave before was approved by the Ministry`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_2/p2
GIVEN h IS A `holiday case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `return to work needs the Ministry's approval` h IF `left without the Ministry's consent` h

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_2/p3 Pointer to entitlement paragraph 3 (substitutes), encoded below.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_2/p4 Pointer to entitlement paragraph 4 (maternity leave), encoded below.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_2/p5 Pointer to entitlement paragraph 5 (reserve duty), encoded below.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_2/p6 Pointer to entitlement paragraph 6 (work accidents), encoded below.

-- §1.25.1 entitlement 3: a substitute of at least 51 days is paid if the days
-- worked before the vacation are not fewer than its days, and the substitute
-- came back the day after it.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_3
GIVEN h IS A `holiday case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the long-substitute rule pays the holiday` h IF
        h's `status for the holiday` EQUALS `a substitute`
    AND h's `days of substitution` AT LEAST 51
    AND h's `workdays before the vacation` AT LEAST h's `days of the holiday vacation`
    AND h's `returned to work the day after the vacation`

-- Second paragraph: a substitute of at least 3 months whose work ended with
-- the end of studies before the holiday is paid, provided the permanent
-- employee returning is not.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_3/p2
GIVEN h IS A `holiday case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ended-substitute rule pays the holiday` h IF
        h's `status for the holiday` EQUALS `a substitute`
    AND h's `months worked before the vacation` AT LEAST 3
    AND h's `work ended with the end of studies before the holiday`
    AND NOT h's `the returning permanent employee is entitled`

@export Whether a teaching employee is paid for a holiday vacation under section 1.25.1 of the takanon
GIVEN h IS A `holiday case` @desc the employee and the holiday
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid for the holiday vacation` h IF
       `the permanent staff rule pays the holiday` h
    OR `approved unpaid leave before the holiday keeps the holiday pay` h
    OR `the long-substitute rule pays the holiday` h
    OR `the ended-substitute rule pays the holiday` h

-- §1.25.1 entitlement 4 and §1.25.5 maternity 4 (the parity committee's
-- decision of 28.1.1971), the same rule twice: on national-insurance
-- maternity leave in the Sukkot, Hanukkah or Passover vacation, salary is paid
-- for the vacation, less the intermediate festival days and Saturdays, on top
-- of the maternity pay.
DECLARE `long holiday vacation` HAS
    `which vacation`                   IS A `kind of vacation`
    `days of the vacation`             IS A NUMBER
    `intermediate festival days and Saturdays in it` IS A NUMBER
    `Saturdays and festival days in it` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN v IS A `long holiday vacation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is Sukkot, Hanukkah or Passover` v IF
       v's `which vacation` EQUALS `the Sukkot vacation`
    OR v's `which vacation` EQUALS `the Hanukkah vacation`
    OR v's `which vacation` EQUALS `the Passover vacation`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_4 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p29
GIVEN v IS A `long holiday vacation`, `daily salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `salary for a vacation on maternity leave` v `daily salary` IS
    IF `is Sukkot, Hanukkah or Passover` v
    THEN `daily salary` TIMES (v's `days of the vacation` MINUS v's `intermediate festival days and Saturdays in it`)
    ELSE 0

-- The note: maternity leave ending on the eve of the vacation or during it
-- gives pay for the whole vacation, if she told the principal and the
-- district's teaching-manpower department in writing, in advance, that she
-- would return straight after it, and did.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_4/p2
GIVEN `maternity leave ended on the eve of the vacation or during it` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave written notice in advance of returning straight after` IS A BOOLEAN, `returned straight after` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid for the whole vacation after maternity leave` `maternity leave ended on the eve of the vacation or during it` `gave written notice in advance of returning straight after` `returned straight after` IF
    `maternity leave ended on the eve of the vacation or during it` AND `gave written notice in advance of returning straight after` AND `returned straight after`

-- §1.25.1 entitlement 5, §1.25.2.7 and §1.25.9.1-2: reserve duty in the
-- Sukkot, Hanukkah or Passover vacation (less the intermediate days and
-- Saturdays) or in the summer vacation is paid from the equalisation fund on
-- top of the vacation pay — §1.25.9.2 adds: for every employee serving then,
-- not only those whose service was deferred at the school's request.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_5 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_9__para_1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_7 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_9__para_2
GIVEN v IS A `long holiday vacation`, `days of reserve duty in the vacation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `reserve days paid from the equalisation fund` v `days of reserve duty in the vacation` IS
    IF `is Sukkot, Hanukkah or Passover` v
    THEN min `days of reserve duty in the vacation` (v's `days of the vacation` MINUS v's `intermediate festival days and Saturdays in it`)
    ELSE IF v's `which vacation` EQUALS `the summer vacation`
         THEN `days of reserve duty in the vacation`
         ELSE 0

-- §1.25.1 entitlement 6: an employee on national-insurance injury pay, whose
-- 27 weeks fall in the Sukkot, Hanukkah or Passover vacation, is paid by the
-- employer for the vacation, less Saturdays and festivals; from 1.9.93.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_2__para_6
GIVEN v IS A `long holiday vacation`, `the 27 weeks of injury pay fall in the vacation` IS A BOOLEAN, `date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `vacation days the employer pays an injured employee` v `the 27 weeks of injury pay fall in the vacation` `date` IS
    IF `is Sukkot, Hanukkah or Passover` v AND `the 27 weeks of injury pay fall in the vacation` AND `date` AT LEAST 19930901
    THEN v's `days of the vacation` MINUS v's `Saturdays and festival days in it`
    ELSE 0

§§ `1.25.1 האחד במאי`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3/p1 Lead-in ("the rules for operating institutions on May Day are as follows").

DECLARE `kind of institution` IS ONE OF
    `a state institution`
    `a state-religious institution`
    `another institution`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3__para_1
GIVEN i IS A `kind of institution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `open on May Day under paragraph 1` i IF TRUE

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3__para_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `vacation action`
DECIDE `no May Day celebrations` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    SHANT `hold a May Day celebration, procession or flag-raising`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.25.1 May Day 2: no May Day celebrations, processions or flags in schools and kindergartens"

-- §1.25.1 May Day 3: a teacher who wishes to celebrate may be absent, after
-- telling the principal in writing in advance; the principal then organises
-- the day, and tells parents in advance of a class that cannot be occupied.
-- F-1.25-a: read as open to teachers of state-religious institutions too.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3__para_3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `vacation action`
DECIDE `a teacher's May Day absence` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `notify the principal in writing of a May Day absence`
    WITHIN 1
    HENCE (PARTY `the teaching employee`
           MAY   `be absent on a school day`)
    LEST  (PARTY `the teaching employee`
           SHANT `be absent on a school day`
           LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.1 May Day 3: a May Day absence needs written notice to the principal in advance")

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3__para_3 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3__para_3/p2
GIVEN `a class cannot be occupied` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `vacation action`
DECIDE `the principal's May Day duties` `a class cannot be occupied` IS
    IF `a class cannot be occupied`
    THEN    (PARTY `the school principal`
             MUST  `organise the school day around the absences`
             WITHIN 1)
         RAND
            (PARTY `the school principal`
             MUST  `notify the parents that a class cannot be occupied`
             WITHIN 1
             LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.25.1 May Day 3: parents are told in advance of a class that cannot be occupied")
    ELSE PARTY `the school principal`
         MUST  `organise the school day around the absences`
         WITHIN 1

-- §1.25.1 May Day 4 and 5: principals, their substitutes and those in charge
-- of security are at their institutions as usual — except that in a
-- settlement where everyone celebrates, the principal (or substitute) may be
-- absent after telling the supervisor in advance.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3__para_4 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3__para_5
GIVEN `the whole settlement celebrates May Day` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `vacation action`
DECIDE `the principal's May Day presence` `the whole settlement celebrates May Day` IS
    IF `the whole settlement celebrates May Day`
    THEN (PARTY `the school principal`
          MUST  `notify the supervisor of a May Day absence`
          WITHIN 1
          HENCE (PARTY `the school principal` MAY `be absent on a school day`)
          LEST  (PARTY `the school principal` MUST `be at the institution as usual` WITHIN 1))
    ELSE PARTY `the school principal`
         MUST  `be at the institution as usual`
         WITHIN 1
         LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.25.1 May Day 4: principals and those in charge of security are at their institutions as usual"

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3__para_6
GIVEN i IS A `kind of institution`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `operates as usual on May Day under paragraph 6` i IF
    i EQUALS `a state-religious institution`

-- F-1.25-a's evidence: paragraph 6 opens no institution paragraph 1 had not
-- already opened, so it either says nothing or limits the teachers'
-- permission in paragraph 3, which it does not name.
`paragraph 6 opens nothing paragraph 1 has not opened` MEANS
    all (GIVEN i YIELD (NOT `operates as usual on May Day under paragraph 6` i) OR `open on May Day under paragraph 1` i)
        (LIST `a state institution`, `a state-religious institution`, `another institution`)
#ASSERT `paragraph 6 opens nothing paragraph 1 has not opened`

§§ `1.25.1 חופשת מפקחים`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3__para_6/p2 Sub-heading ("inspectors' leave").

DECLARE `fixed inspectors' leave day` IS ONE OF
    `the eve of Passover`
    `the eve of Shavuot`
    `the eve of Rosh Hashana`
    `the eve of Yom Kippur`
    `the eve of Sukkot`
    `an intermediate day of Passover`

-- Ten days on fixed dates, on top of the regular leave, never accumulated and
-- never exchanged. The five eves and the intermediate days of Passover make
-- the ten; how many intermediate days a year has is a calendar input.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3__para_6/p3
GIVEN `intermediate days of Passover that year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `inspectors' fixed leave days` `intermediate days of Passover that year` IS
    min 10 (5 PLUS `intermediate days of Passover that year`)

`inspectors' fixed leave carries over` MEANS FALSE

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3__para_6/p3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `vacation action`
DECIDE `the fixed days are not exchanged` IS
    PARTY `the supervisor`
    SHANT `exchange a fixed inspectors' leave day for another day`
    WITHIN 12
    LEST  BREACH BY `the supervisor` BECAUSE "section 1.25.1: the inspectors' fixed leave days may not be exchanged for others"

-- A teacher in an instructing role has the leave customary for inspectors and
-- instructors, in proportion to the position.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1__hc_3__para_6/p4
GIVEN `leave days customary for inspectors and instructors` IS A NUMBER, `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `an instructing teacher's leave days` `leave days customary for inspectors and instructors` `position fraction` IS
    `leave days customary for inspectors and instructors` TIMES `position fraction`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p1 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p2 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p3 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p4 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p5 Source list: a letter of the assistant for conditions of service.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p6 Source list: a parity committee decision.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p7 Source list: a parity committee decision.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p8 Source list: Director-General's circulars.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p9 Source list: a letter and a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p10 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p11 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p12 Source list: a wage agreement and an education-administration circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_1/p13 Source list: a Director-General's circular.

-- Examples (placeholder figures).
`a permanent teacher who worked before Passover` MEANS
    `holiday case` `on the permanent staff` `a day of work` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE
`a permanent teacher on unapproved unpaid leave` MEANS
    `holiday case` `on the permanent staff` `unpaid leave` FALSE FALSE 0 0 0 TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE
`a permanent teacher on approved unpaid leave` MEANS
    `holiday case` `on the permanent staff` `unpaid leave` FALSE TRUE 0 0 0 TRUE 0 FALSE FALSE
`a 60-day substitute` MEANS
    `holiday case` `a substitute` `a day of work` FALSE FALSE 60 40 10 TRUE 3 FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `paid for the holiday vacation` `a permanent teacher who worked before Passover`
#ASSERT NOT `paid for the holiday vacation` `a permanent teacher on unapproved unpaid leave`
#ASSERT `return to work needs the Ministry's approval` `a permanent teacher on unapproved unpaid leave`
#ASSERT `paid for the holiday vacation` `a permanent teacher on approved unpaid leave`
#ASSERT `paid for the holiday vacation` `a 60-day substitute`

`a ten-day Passover vacation` MEANS
    `long holiday vacation` `the Passover vacation` 10 6 3
#ASSERT `salary for a vacation on maternity leave` `a ten-day Passover vacation` 100 EQUALS 400
#ASSERT `sick days charged for illness in a vacation` `the Passover vacation` TRUE 3 EQUALS 0

#TRACE `presence on school days` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `request a permit to be absent` AT 1

§§ `1.25.2 חופשת הקיץ`

DECLARE `stratum for the summer` IS ONE OF
    `kindergartens and elementary institutions`
    `post-primary institutions, teacher-training institutions and youth centres`

-- §1.25.2.1א-ב: when the summer vacation runs, as MMDD numbers.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_1__subpara_a akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_1__subpara_b
GIVEN s IS A `stratum for the summer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `summer vacation starts (MMDD)` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `kindergartens and elementary institutions` THEN 701
    WHEN `post-primary institutions, teacher-training institutions and youth centres` THEN 620

`summer vacation ends (MMDD)` MEANS 831

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_1__subpara_c Pointer to the Ministry's yearly circulars on the arrangements of each kind of institution; no rule of its own.

@desc A teaching employee's school year, as the summer-vacation pay of section 1.25.2 asks about it.
DECLARE `summer case` HAS
    `summer stratum`                      IS A `stratum for the summer`
    `regular or substitute`               IS A `staff status`
    `longest run of consecutive workdays` IS A NUMBER
    `months taught in the year`           IS A NUMBER @desc months the employee actually taught in the school year
    `months worked in the year`           IS A NUMBER @desc work months of the school year, before the periods sections 1.25.2.6-8 count as work
    `months of maternity leave with national-insurance pay` IS A NUMBER
    `months absent after an injury on a school trip, on injury pay` IS A NUMBER
    `summer position fraction`            IS A NUMBER @desc the share of a position held in the year, above one position too (section 1.25.2.4)
    `daily salary of a full position`     IS A NUMBER @desc an input set by the salary scales

-- §1.25.2.2א: a regular employee or substitute employed for MORE than 51
-- consecutive workdays is paid in the summer, provided they taught at least
-- two months of the year.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_2__subpara_a
GIVEN c IS A `summer case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to summer-vacation pay` c IF
        c's `longest run of consecutive workdays` GREATER THAN 51
    AND c's `months taught in the year` AT LEAST 2

-- §1.25.2.2ב: the quota is 6 days per month of work in elementary education
-- and 7 in post-primary.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_2__subpara_b
GIVEN s IS A `stratum for the summer`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `summer days per month of work` s IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `kindergartens and elementary institutions` THEN 6
    WHEN `post-primary institutions, teacher-training institutions and youth centres` THEN 7

-- §§1.25.2.6 and 8: maternity leave on national-insurance pay, and absence
-- after an injury on a school trip on injury pay, count as work.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_6 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_8
GIVEN c IS A `summer case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months of work for the summer` c IS
      c's `months worked in the year`
    PLUS c's `months of maternity leave with national-insurance pay`
    PLUS c's `months absent after an injury on a school trip, on injury pay`

-- §1.25.2.4: work above one full position is paid in the summer too, so the
-- position fraction is not capped at one.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_4
GIVEN c IS A `summer case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `position fraction paid in the summer` c IS c's `summer position fraction`

@export Summer-vacation pay of a teaching employee under section 1.25.2 of the takanon
GIVEN c IS A `summer case` @desc the employee's school year
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `summer-vacation pay` c IS
    IF `entitled to summer-vacation pay` c
    THEN `summer days per month of work` (c's `summer stratum`)
         TIMES `months of work for the summer` c
         TIMES c's `daily salary of a full position`
         TIMES `position fraction paid in the summer` c
    ELSE 0

-- §1.25.2.3: an employee (other than a principal) who works in the summer
-- with the Ministry's approval is paid in addition; the amount is an input.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_3
GIVEN `is a principal` IS A BOOLEAN, `worked in the summer with the Ministry's approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `the additional payment for summer work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `additional payment for work in the summer` `is a principal` `worked in the summer with the Ministry's approval` `the additional payment for summer work` IS
    IF `worked in the summer with the Ministry's approval` AND NOT `is a principal`
    THEN `the additional payment for summer work`
    ELSE 0

-- §1.25.2.5 and §1.25.5 maternity 5, the same rule twice: on maternity leave
-- in the summer, she is paid her regular salary and, on top of it, the
-- maternity pay is made up to two months' salary.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_5 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p30
GIVEN `monthly salary` IS A NUMBER, `maternity pay received for the summer` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `summer top-up of maternity pay` `monthly salary` `maternity pay received for the summer` IS
    max 0 (2 TIMES `monthly salary` MINUS `maternity pay received for the summer`)

-- §1.25.2.6א: a teacher on a study-fund sabbatical who gave birth during it
-- or at its end has the sabbatical counted as a year of work for every purpose.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_6/p2
GIVEN `on a study-fund sabbatical` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave birth during it or at its end` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sabbatical counts as a year of work` `on a study-fund sabbatical` `gave birth during it or at its end` IF
    `on a study-fund sabbatical` AND `gave birth during it or at its end`

-- §1.25.2.9: injured in a work accident before the summer and still ill from it
-- in the vacation, the employee is paid for the vacation as if healthy, and is
-- also entitled to injury pay if national insurance recognised the claim.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_9
GIVEN `summer pay as if healthy` IS A NUMBER, `injury pay recognised by national insurance` IS A NUMBER, `national insurance recognised the right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `income in the summer after a work accident` `summer pay as if healthy` `injury pay recognised by national insurance` `national insurance recognised the right` IS
    IF `national insurance recognised the right`
    THEN `summer pay as if healthy` PLUS `injury pay recognised by national insurance`
    ELSE `summer pay as if healthy`

-- §1.25.2.10: teachers whom their role keeps at school in the vacations and
-- who are injured performing it are entitled to injury pay (a work
-- accident); the second paragraph: an employee injured in the summer
-- vacation has no work accident, and is treated as one ill in the summer,
-- paid as if healthy. F-1.25-b: the two disagree on a teacher injured on
-- duty in the summer. The reading adopted: the first paragraph, the specific
-- one, governs those required to be at school and injured on duty.
@desc An accident in a vacation, as section 1.25.2.10 asks about it.
DECLARE `vacation accident` HAS
    `in the summer vacation`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the role requires presence at school in the vacations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `injured while performing the role`   IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_10
GIVEN a IS A `vacation accident`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `what the first paragraph says of a work accident` a IS
    IF a's `the role requires presence at school in the vacations` AND a's `injured while performing the role`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_10/p2
GIVEN a IS A `vacation accident`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `what the second paragraph says of a work accident` a IS
    IF a's `in the summer vacation`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- The adopted reading: the first paragraph where it speaks, then the second;
-- where neither speaks the section does not decide, and this file says no.
GIVEN a IS A `vacation accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a work accident in the vacation` a IS
    fromMaybe FALSE (orElse (`what the first paragraph says of a work accident` a) (`what the second paragraph says of a work accident` a))

GIVEN a IS A `vacation accident`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid as one ill in the summer, as if healthy` a IF
    a's `in the summer vacation` AND NOT `a work accident in the vacation` a

`a teacher injured on duty in the summer` MEANS
    `vacation accident` TRUE TRUE TRUE
`the two paragraphs disagree on an on-duty summer accident` MEANS
    `what the first paragraph says of a work accident` `a teacher injured on duty in the summer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    AND `what the second paragraph says of a work accident` `a teacher injured on duty in the summer` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the two paragraphs disagree on an on-duty summer accident`
#ASSERT `a work accident in the vacation` `a teacher injured on duty in the summer`
#ASSERT `paid as one ill in the summer, as if healthy` (`vacation accident` TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2__para_11 Pointer to section 1.25.1's entitlement paragraphs for leave before and after the summer, encoded above.

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2/p1 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2/p2 Source list: letters of the officer for service regulations.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2/p3 Source list: a letter of the assistant for conditions of service.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2/p4 Source list: a letter of the officer for conditions of service.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2/p5 Source list: a special Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2/p6 Source list: the civil-service regulations and the local-authority labour code, and a circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2/p7 Source list: Director-General's circulars.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2/p8 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2/p9 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_2/p10 Source list: a supreme parity committee decision and the Ministry accountant's approval.

-- Examples. The daily salary of 100 is a placeholder.
`an elementary teacher, a full year` MEANS
    `summer case` `kindergartens and elementary institutions` `on the permanent staff` 180 10 9 1 0 1 100
#ASSERT `months of work for the summer` `an elementary teacher, a full year` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `summer-vacation pay` `an elementary teacher, a full year` EQUALS 6000
`a 40-day substitute` MEANS
    `summer case` `post-primary institutions, teacher-training institutions and youth centres` `a substitute` 40 2 2 0 0 1 100
#ASSERT `summer-vacation pay` `a 40-day substitute` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `summer top-up of maternity pay` 10000 15000 EQUALS 5000

§§ `1.25.3.1 חופשת מחלה — זכאות`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p1 Amendment note ("this section was updated on 6.11.03").

-- The opening paragraph: under the 1.9.58 collective agreement the civil
-- service regulations apply, giving 30 days of sick leave a year — "or in
-- hours, four times the position base". The two measures are one: 30 days
-- equal four bases of hours, which is also the rate at which a year-end
-- surplus of hours turns into days (paragraph 1ב below).
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p2
`sick-leave days a year` MEANS 30

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p2
`bases of hours in a year's sick leave` MEANS 4

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p3 Heading of clause 1 ("illness").

DECLARE `sick-leave action` IS ONE OF
    `notify the principal of a sick absence at the start of its first day`
    `deliver the declaration and the medical confirmation`
    `report the illness to the study fund, with medical certificates`
    `report the illness to the owner the sabbatical was taken from`
    `pay salary charged to accumulated sick days` HAS `sick salary paid` IS A NUMBER
    `stop the monthly study grant`
    `apply for half-pay sick leave on the employee's behalf`
    `decide on half-pay sick leave`
    `certify the unused sick days`
    `pay salary for the certified unused sick days`
    `reimburse the current employer`

-- Clause 1א: illness is the temporary or permanent inability to do the work
-- that follows, on medical findings, from ill health; it gives sick leave
-- whatever its cause (ordinary illness, a high-risk pregnancy, IVF, an
-- accident outside work hours), on a doctor's signed certificate.
DECLARE `cause of illness` IS ONE OF
    `ordinary illness`
    `keeping a pregnancy`
    `in-vitro fertilisation`
    `an accident outside working hours`
    `another cause`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p4
GIVEN `unable to work on medical findings` IS A BOOLEAN, `brought a certificate signed by a doctor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to sick leave` `unable to work on medical findings` `brought a certificate signed by a doctor` IF
    `unable to work on medical findings` AND `brought a certificate signed by a doctor`

-- The notice: at the start of the first day of absence, to the principal (by
-- a relative or another person if the employee cannot); a kindergarten
-- teacher to the official the district appoints or her supervisor. Time in days.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p4
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sick-leave action`
DECIDE `notice of a sick absence` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `notify the principal of a sick absence at the start of its first day`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.3.1(1)(a): a sick absence is notified at the start of its first day"

-- Clause 1ב: the year's "sick-day hours" are four times the position base,
-- in proportion to the year's extent of employment (above one position too).
-- The year's absences from the fixed timetable are set off against them, and
-- the surplus becomes days at the year's end, carried from year to year.
@desc A teaching employee's sick-day hours for one school year.
DECLARE `sick-hours year` HAS
    `position base hours`                  IS A NUMBER @desc the weekly hours of the employee's position base (an input)
    `extent of employment in the year`     IS A NUMBER @desc the year's share of a position, above one included
    `hours absent from the fixed timetable` IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p5
GIVEN y IS A `sick-hours year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick-day hours of the year` y IS
    `bases of hours in a year's sick leave` TIMES y's `position base hours` TIMES y's `extent of employment in the year`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p6 Announces examples ("below are a few examples") that the corpus text does not carry; a lost table is the corpus's to fix, and nothing here is a rule.

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p7
GIVEN y IS A `sick-hours year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `surplus sick-day hours` y IS
    max 0 (`sick-day hours of the year` y MINUS y's `hours absent from the fixed timetable`)

-- The paragraph does not state the rate of conversion; the opening paragraph's
-- equation of 30 days with four bases of hours is used for it.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p8
GIVEN y IS A `sick-hours year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick days credited at the year's end` y IS
    IF y's `position base hours` TIMES y's `extent of employment in the year` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE `surplus sick-day hours` y TIMES `sick-leave days a year`
         DIVIDED BY `sick-day hours of the year` y

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p8
`credited sick days carry over to the next year` MEANS TRUE

-- Clause 1ג: on sick leave the employee is paid what would have been earned
-- working, and the period counts as work for every purpose (see clause 13).
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p9
GIVEN `salary had the employee worked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `salary on sick leave` `salary had the employee worked` IS `salary had the employee worked`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p10 Pointer to clause 12 (illness in a sabbatical year), encoded below.

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p11 Heading of clause 2 ("declaration days").

-- Clause 2: absence for illness of one or two consecutive days without a
-- medical certificate, on a personal declaration, twice a school year. A
-- single day twice uses up the year's declaration days.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p12 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p13
GIVEN `lengths of the declared absences` IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the declared absences are within the declaration days` `lengths of the declared absences` IF
        count `lengths of the declared absences` AT MOST 2
    AND all (GIVEN d YIELD d AT LEAST 1 AND d AT MOST 2) `lengths of the declared absences`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p14 Heading of clause 3 ("absence for a child's illness").

@desc The family circumstances clauses 3 to 6 of section 1.25.3.1 ask about.
DECLARE `family circumstances` HAS
    `the spouse is an employee who did not take this absence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the spouse is self-employed and did not leave the business for it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the employee's sole custody`          IS A BOOLEAN
    `a single parent`                         IS A BOOLEAN @desc הורה עצמאי as the Single-Parent Families Law 1992 defines it
    `years with this employer`                IS A NUMBER
    `another person used the additional days for the same person` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days already charged under clause 3`     IS A NUMBER
    `days already charged under clauses 3 and 3a for the disabled child` IS A NUMBER

-- Clause 3: a child under 16 — up to 8 days a year where the spouse works
-- (or is self-employed) and did not take the absence; up to 16 where the
-- child is in the employee's sole custody or the employee is a single parent.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p15 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p16 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p17 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p18
GIVEN `age of the child` IS A NUMBER, f IS A `family circumstances`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days a year for a child's illness` `age of the child` f IS
    IF `age of the child` AT LEAST 16
    THEN 0
    ELSE BRANCH IF f's `in the employee's sole custody` OR f's `a single parent` THEN 16
                IF f's `the spouse is an employee who did not take this absence`
                   OR f's `the spouse is self-employed and did not leave the business for it` THEN 8
                OTHERWISE 0

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p19 Heading of clause 3א ("absence for a child's malignant illness").

-- Clause 3א: a child under 18, after a year with the employer — up to 90 days
-- a year (charged to sick leave or vacation, as the employee chooses); 110
-- where the spouse works and did not take the absence or the child is in sole
-- custody. Days charged under clause 3 count towards it.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p20 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p21 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p22
GIVEN `age of the child` IS A NUMBER, f IS A `family circumstances`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days left for a child's malignant illness` `age of the child` f IS
    IF `age of the child` AT LEAST 18 OR f's `years with this employer` LESS THAN 1
    THEN 0
    ELSE max 0 (`ceiling` MINUS f's `days already charged under clause 3`)
    WHERE
        `ceiling` MEANS
            IF f's `the spouse is an employee who did not take this absence` OR f's `in the employee's sole custody`
            THEN 110
            ELSE 90

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p23 Heading of clause 3ב ("absence to give personal assistance to a person with a disability").

-- Clause 3ב(א): a parent of a person with a disability, after a year with the
-- employer — up to 18 days a year, and up to 15 more if one of (1)-(4) holds
-- and no other person used the additional days for the same person. Item (3)
-- prints "הוא הורה עצמאי(4) האדם עם המוגבלות נמצא בהחזקתו הבלעדית": read as two
-- items, (3) a single parent and (4) sole custody.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p24 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p25 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p26 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p27
GIVEN f IS A `family circumstances`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the additional disability days are open` f IF
        (   f's `the spouse is an employee who did not take this absence`
         OR f's `the spouse is self-employed and did not leave the business for it`
         OR f's `a single parent`
         OR f's `in the employee's sole custody`)
    AND NOT f's `another person used the additional days for the same person`

-- Clause 3ב(ג): days charged under clauses 3 and 3א for the same disabled child count.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p24 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p29
GIVEN f IS A `family circumstances`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days left for assisting a person with a disability` f IS
    IF f's `years with this employer` LESS THAN 1
    THEN 0
    ELSE max 0 ((18 PLUS (IF `the additional disability days are open` f THEN 15 ELSE 0))
                MINUS f's `days already charged under clauses 3 and 3a for the disabled child`)

-- Clause 3ב(ב): the same for a guardian of a person with a disability, if no
-- one else cares for that person and no other guardian used the right.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p28
GIVEN `no other person cares for the person` IS A BOOLEAN, `no other guardian used the right` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a guardian has the disability days` `no other person cares for the person` `no other guardian used the right` IF
    `no other person cares for the person` AND `no other guardian used the right`

-- Clause 3ב(ד): the two terms are the Equal Rights for Persons with
-- Disabilities Law's (section 5) and personal assistance (supervision,
-- escort, care); both are facts given to the rules above.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p30 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p31
DECLARE `personal assistance` IS ONE OF
    supervision
    escort
    care
    `other assistance the person needs because of the disability`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p32 Heading of clause 3ג ("family and foster care").

-- Clause 3ג: clauses 3 to 3ב apply to a foster parent, but the days are
-- charged only if the natural or adoptive parent did not use the right on
-- those days. A foster family is one approved by whom the welfare minister
-- empowers.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p33
GIVEN `a foster parent in an approved foster family` IS A BOOLEAN, `the natural or adoptive parent used the right on those days` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a foster parent's days are charged` `a foster parent in an approved foster family` `the natural or adoptive parent used the right on those days` IF
    `a foster parent in an approved foster family` AND NOT `the natural or adoptive parent used the right on those days`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p34 Heading ("the employee's declaration").

-- Clause 3's declaration: signed by the employee and the spouse (only the
-- employee where the child is in sole custody), with a medical confirmation;
-- until delivered, the absence is not one under clause 3. The same shape
-- governs clauses 4, 5 and 6 below.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p35
GIVEN `the declaration was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN, `signed by the spouse or not needed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the medical confirmation was attached` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the absence counts under clause 3` `the declaration was delivered` `signed by the spouse or not needed` `the medical confirmation was attached` IF
    `the declaration was delivered` AND `signed by the spouse or not needed` AND `the medical confirmation was attached`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p35 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p45 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p52 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p58
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sick-leave action`
DECIDE `delivering the declaration` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `deliver the declaration and the medical confirmation`

-- Clauses 3, 4 and 5 each say the workplace's rules on notifying an absence
-- for illness are not displaced; they are the notice rule of clause 1א above.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p36 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p46 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p53
`the workplace's notice rules still apply to family absences` MEANS `notice of a sick absence`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p37 Heading of clause 4 ("absence for the illness of a parent or a spouse's parent").

-- Clause 4: up to 6 days a year of actual absence for the illness of the
-- employee's or the spouse's parent, charged to accumulated sick leave,
-- provided the spouse is an employee who did not take the absence "under this
-- law". F-1.25-c: the clause speaks of "this law" and "section 1 of the Law"
-- and names no law; read as the clause's own grant (clause 4א).
@desc A parent's illness, as clause 4 of section 1.25.3.1 asks about it.
DECLARE `parent's illness` HAS
    `the parent is wholly dependent on others for daily activities` IS A BOOLEAN @desc dressing, eating, continence, washing, moving about the home
    `the parent is in a nursing institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a sibling took the absence for the same matter and period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a brother or sister of the employee as a child (adopted included) of that parent
    `the spouse is an employee who did not take the absence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the parent's doctor confirmed the dependence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a signed declaration was delivered` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p38 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p40 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p41 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p42 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p43 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p44 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p45
GIVEN p IS A `parent's illness`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days a year for a parent's illness` p IS
    IF     p's `the parent is wholly dependent on others for daily activities`
       AND p's `the spouse is an employee who did not take the absence`
       AND NOT p's `the parent is in a nursing institution`
       AND NOT p's `a sibling took the absence for the same matter and period`
       AND p's `the parent's doctor confirmed the dependence`
       AND p's `a signed declaration was delivered`
    THEN 6
    ELSE 0

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p39
`the parent-illness amendment applies from` MEANS 20140213

-- F-1.25-c's evidence: the laws the text of clause 4 names (none) against the
-- references it makes to "this law" and "section 1 of the Law".
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `the laws clause 4 names in its text` IS EMPTY
`clause 4's references to "the Law"` MEANS LIST "לפי חוק זה", "תחילתו של תיקון חוק זה", "לענין חוק זה", "מכוח סעיף 1 לחוק", "כאמור בסעיף 1 לחוק", "המזכה מכוח סעיף 1 לחוק"
`clause 4 refers to a law it never names` MEANS
    count `clause 4's references to "the Law"` GREATER THAN 0 AND null `the laws clause 4 names in its text`
#ASSERT `clause 4 refers to a law it never names`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p47 Heading of clause 5 ("absence for a spouse's illness").

-- Clause 5א: up to 6 days a year for a spouse's illness, on a signed
-- declaration to the principal with the spouse's doctor's confirmation that
-- the spouse is wholly dependent on others for daily activities; until
-- delivered, the absence is not lawful.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p48 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p49 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p50 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p51 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p52
GIVEN `the spouse is wholly dependent on others for daily activities` IS A BOOLEAN, `declaration and doctor's confirmation delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days a year for a spouse's illness` `the spouse is wholly dependent on others for daily activities` `declaration and doctor's confirmation delivered` IS
    IF `the spouse is wholly dependent on others for daily activities` AND `declaration and doctor's confirmation delivered`
    THEN 6
    ELSE 0

-- Clause 5ב: a spouse's malignant illness, after a year in the service — up to
-- 60 days a year, counting days charged under 5א.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p54 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p55
GIVEN `years in the service` IS A NUMBER, `days charged under clause 5a` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days left for a spouse's malignant illness` `years in the service` `days charged under clause 5a` IS
    IF `years in the service` AT LEAST 1
    THEN max 0 (60 MINUS `days charged under clause 5a`)
    ELSE 0

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p56 Heading of clause 6 ("absence for pregnancy and birth").

-- Clause 6: up to 7 days a year for a partner's pregnancy treatments or tests,
-- or her giving birth, on a declaration (form 1.25.3.7) with her doctor's
-- confirmation; an absence qualifies only if it is one of the three listed.
DECLARE `reason for a partner's-pregnancy absence` IS ONE OF
    `escorting her to pregnancy treatments or tests that risk her life or the foetus's` @desc and, after an abortion, up to 24 hours from its end
    `escorting her where she depends on another's help for the treatments or tests`
    `being present at the birth` @desc from the onset of labour to 24 hours after the birth
    `another reason`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p57 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p58 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p59 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p60 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p61 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p62
GIVEN r IS A `reason for a partner's-pregnancy absence`, `documents delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a qualifying partner's-pregnancy absence` r `documents delivered` IF
    `documents delivered` AND NOT r EQUALS `another reason`

`days a year for a partner's pregnancy and birth` MEANS 7

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p62
`the partner's-pregnancy rule applies from` MEANS 20000706

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p63 Heading of clause 7 ("use of sick days by an official-education employee disqualified for health reasons").

-- Clause 7: an employee disqualified from service for health reasons may use
-- the accumulated sick days, by the disability fixed: 100% — all of them;
-- 51% to 99% — that percentage of them; up to 50% — none (unused days are
-- paid under the civil service regulations, 33.271), unless the teaching-
-- manpower division allows a wholly incapacitated, housebound employee to use
-- them. In every case salary stops at 65. From 1.11.91.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p64 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p65 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p67
GIVEN `disability percent` IS A NUMBER, `accumulated sick days` IS A NUMBER, `the division allowed days under paragraph (d)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick days a disqualified employee may use` `disability percent` `accumulated sick days` `the division allowed days under paragraph (d)` IS
    BRANCH IF `disability percent` AT LEAST 100 THEN `accumulated sick days`
           IF `disability percent` AT LEAST 51 THEN `disability percent` DIVIDED BY 100 TIMES `accumulated sick days`
           OTHERWISE `the division allowed days under paragraph (d)`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p64 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p65
GIVEN `days the employee may use` IS A NUMBER, `days until the employee is 65` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days of salary before retirement` `days the employee may use` `days until the employee is 65` IS
    min `days the employee may use` `days until the employee is 65`

-- The worked example of clause 7ב: 60% disability, 100 days, age 58 — 60 days.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p66
`the clause 7b example's days` MEANS
    `days of salary before retirement` (`sick days a disqualified employee may use` 60 100 0) (7 TIMES 365)
#ASSERT `the clause 7b example's days` EQUALS 60

-- Clause 7ד: a disqualified employee with up to 50% who is wholly unable to
-- work and confined to home or bed may ask the division, which decides.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p68
GIVEN `disability percent` IS A NUMBER, `wholly unable to work and confined, on medical confirmation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.25 party` `sick-leave action`
DECIDE `the division's decision on a disqualified employee's days` `disability percent` `wholly unable to work and confined, on medical confirmation` IS
    IF `disability percent` AT MOST 50 AND `wholly unable to work and confined, on medical confirmation`
    THEN PARTY `the teaching-manpower division`
         MAY   `decide on half-pay sick leave`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- The paragraph after 7ד keeps the right to payment for unused sick leave
-- where it is larger than the salary for using them, or where the employee
-- chooses to retire at once. F-1.25-d: it calls the options "the options
-- listed in section 2 above"; clause 2 is the declaration days, and the
-- options are 7א-7ד.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p69
GIVEN `salary for using the days` IS A NUMBER, `payment for unused sick days` IS A NUMBER, `chose to retire at once` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `what a disqualified employee receives for the days` `salary for using the days` `payment for unused sick days` `chose to retire at once` IS
    IF `chose to retire at once`
    THEN `payment for unused sick days`
    ELSE max `salary for using the days` `payment for unused sick days`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p70
`the disqualification rule applies from` MEANS 19911101

DECLARE `clause of section 1.25.3.1` HAS
    `clause number` IS A STRING
    `clause subject` IS A STRING

`the clauses of section 1.25.3.1` MEANS
    LIST `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "1"  "illness",
         `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "2"  "declaration days",
         `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "3"  "a child's illness",
         `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "4"  "a parent's illness",
         `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "5"  "a spouse's illness",
         `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "6"  "pregnancy and birth",
         `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "7"  "use of sick days on disqualification for health reasons",
         `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "8"  "half-pay sick leave",
         `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "9"  "the sick-days fund",
         `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "11" "miscellaneous",
         `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "12" "illness in a sabbatical year",
         `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "13" "sick leave as a period of work",
         `clause of section 1.25.3.1` "14" "carrying sick days over"

GIVEN n IS A STRING
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `subject of clause` n IS
    map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `clause subject`) (filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `clause number` EQUALS n) `the clauses of section 1.25.3.1`)

`"section 2 above" in clause 7 is the declaration days` MEANS
    `subject of clause` "2" EQUALS LIST "declaration days"
#ASSERT `"section 2 above" in clause 7 is the declaration days`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p71 Heading of clause 8 ("sick leave at half salary").

-- Clause 8: the Civil Service Commissioner delegated (4.10.78) to the head of
-- the teaching-manpower division the power to approve further sick leave at
-- half salary, for up to 3 months. The principal applies, with a medical
-- certificate, for an employee who used all sick days and is still ill; the
-- head approves where the employee has 3 years in the civil service
-- (temporary service included), has used all annual leave, and — F-1.25-e —
-- was not given 3 months of it in the last two years. The bar is read as
-- applying to any earlier approval, not only to one of a full 3 months.
@desc An application for half-pay sick leave under clause 8.
DECLARE `half-pay application` HAS
    `used all sick days and still ill` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years in the civil service`       IS A NUMBER @desc temporary service included
    `used all annual leave`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `months since an earlier half-pay approval` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc NOTHING when there was none
    `months of the earlier approval`   IS A NUMBER
    `months asked for`                 IS A NUMBER

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p72
`most months of half-pay sick leave` MEANS 3

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p72 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p73 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p75 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p76 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p77 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p78
GIVEN a IS A `half-pay application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `half-pay sick leave may be approved` a IF
        a's `used all sick days and still ill`
    AND a's `years in the civil service` AT LEAST 3
    AND a's `used all annual leave`
    AND a's `months asked for` AT MOST `most months of half-pay sick leave`
    AND `no earlier approval within two years` a

GIVEN a IS A `half-pay application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `no earlier approval within two years` a IF
    CONSIDER a's `months since an earlier half-pay approval`
    WHEN JUST m THEN m AT LEAST 24
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p74
GIVEN a IS A `half-pay application`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sick-leave action`
DECIDE `the principal applies for half-pay sick leave` a IS
    IF a's `used all sick days and still ill`
    THEN PARTY `the school principal`
         MUST  `apply for half-pay sick leave on the employee's behalf`
         WITHIN 30
         LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.25.3.1(8)(b)(1): the principal applies, with a medical certificate, for an employee who used all sick days"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- F-1.25-e's evidence: the bar names an earlier approval "for 3 months"; on
-- its words an employee given ONE month a year ago is not barred, and one
-- given three is — the text does not say which way a shorter one goes.
GIVEN `months of the earlier approval` IS A NUMBER, `months since it` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `barred on the clause's words` `months of the earlier approval` `months since it` IF
    `months of the earlier approval` EQUALS 3 AND `months since it` LESS THAN 24

`the two-year bar's words reach only an earlier approval of 3 months` MEANS
    `barred on the clause's words` 3 12 AND NOT `barred on the clause's words` 1 12
#ASSERT `the two-year bar's words reach only an earlier approval of 3 months`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p79 Heading of clause 9 ("the sick-days fund for official-education teaching employees — excerpts from the agreements").

§§ `1.25.3.1(9) קרן ימי מחלה`

-- The fund pays grants in illness under the agreement's rules (1(א));
-- "illness" is as civil-service regulation 33.204 defines it (1(ב)), a fact
-- given to it.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p80 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p81
`the fund pays grants to employees in illness` MEANS TRUE

-- 2(א): a one-time 1% of the national-insurance base salary, translated into
-- "work hours" at the first-year certified teacher's grade on a 30-hour
-- position; 3: the fund holds those hours, linked to that teacher's salary.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p82
GIVEN `national-insurance base salary` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `one-time contribution to the fund` `national-insurance base salary` IS
    1% TIMES `national-insurance base salary`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p82 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p84
GIVEN `contributions collected` IS A NUMBER, `hourly salary of a first-year certified teacher on 30 hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `work hours in the fund` `contributions collected` `hourly salary of a first-year certified teacher on 30 hours` IS
    `contributions collected` DIVIDED BY `hourly salary of a first-year certified teacher on 30 hours`

-- 2(ב): the table of absolute weights of the grades, kept by the Ministry and
-- published in the Director-General's circular, is the basis of the fund's
-- accounts; it is an input.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p83
GIVEN `the weight of the employee's grade in the published table` IS A NUMBER, `work hours` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `work hours weighted by grade` `the weight of the employee's grade in the published table` `work hours` IS
    `work hours` TIMES `the weight of the employee's grade in the published table`

@desc An employee asking the sick-days fund for a grant.
DECLARE `fund application` HAS
    `used the accumulated sick leave, carried days included` IS A BOOLEAN
    `employment status for the fund`    IS A `status for the fund`
    `completed a year of actual teaching` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in an employer's service the day the sick days ran out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc a substitute on a monthly salary included
    `consecutive days absent ill after the sick days ran out` IS A NUMBER
    `was given special sick leave by the state` IS A BOOLEAN
    `used that special sick leave`       IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `status for the fund` IS ONE OF
    permanent
    temporary
    `on a special contract`
    `other status`

-- 4: the fund may give a grant if all of 4א-4ה hold. F-1.25-f: 4ה speaks of
-- the special sick leave "under section 10 below"; it is read as clause 7's
-- half-pay leave.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p85 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p86 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p87 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p88 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p89 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p90
GIVEN a IS A `fund application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the fund may give a grant` a IF
        a's `used the accumulated sick leave, carried days included`
    AND (NOT a's `employment status for the fund` EQUALS `other status`)
    AND a's `completed a year of actual teaching`
    AND a's `in an employer's service the day the sick days ran out`
    AND a's `consecutive days absent ill after the sick days ran out` AT LEAST 7
    AND (a's `used that special sick leave` OR NOT a's `was given special sick leave by the state`)

-- 5 and 8: the grant weighs the employee's economic and social situation, is
-- at most 100% of salary, computed on the salary of ordinary paid sick leave.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p91 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p94
GIVEN `grant the fund decides on` IS A NUMBER, `salary as on ordinary paid sick leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the fund's monthly grant` `grant the fund decides on` `salary as on ordinary paid sick leave` IS
    min `grant the fund decides on` `salary as on ordinary paid sick leave`

-- 6: the grant period is "as a rule" at most 3 consecutive months; the
-- exception is the fund's to make. F-1.25-f: it says "under section 7",
-- where clause 7 is the half-pay leave outside the fund.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p92
GIVEN `months asked` IS A NUMBER, `the fund makes an exception` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the grant period is allowed` `months asked` `the fund makes an exception` IF
    `months asked` AT MOST 3 OR `the fund makes an exception`

-- 7: the agreement does not take away half-pay sick leave on the Treasury's
-- account, ex gratia, for up to 3 months with the Commission's special approval.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p93
`the fund leaves the Treasury's half-pay leave in place` MEANS TRUE

-- 9: the grant period is unpaid sick leave; it counts for seniority
-- (civil-service regulation 33.215) but not for severance pay or pension.
DECLARE `purpose a period counts for` IS ONE OF
    `seniority`
    `severance pay`
    `pension`
    `sick-day accrual`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p95
GIVEN p IS A `purpose a period counts for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a fund-grant period counts for` p IF
    p EQUALS `seniority`

-- 10(א): the application is on a special form, through the employee's
-- teachers' organisation, the district office (state employees) or the employer.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p96
DECLARE `channel for a fund application` IS ONE OF
    `the employee's teachers' organisation`
    `the district office, for state employees`
    `the employer concerned`

-- F-1.25-f's evidence: the excerpt's own clauses, by number and subject, and
-- what its three internal references find there.
DECLARE `fund clause` HAS
    `fund clause number` IS A NUMBER
    `fund clause subject` IS A STRING

`the clauses of the fund excerpt` MEANS
    LIST `fund clause` 1  "the fund and the meaning of illness",
         `fund clause` 2  "the contribution and the weights table",
         `fund clause` 3  "the hours the fund holds",
         `fund clause` 4  "the conditions of a grant",
         `fund clause` 5  "the size of a grant",
         `fund clause` 6  "the period of grants",
         `fund clause` 7  "half-pay leave on the Treasury's account",
         `fund clause` 8  "the salary a grant is computed on",
         `fund clause` 9  "the grant period's status",
         `fund clause` 10 "the application form"

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
DECIDE `fund clause subject of` n IS
    map (GIVEN c YIELD c's `fund clause subject`) (filter (GIVEN c YIELD c's `fund clause number` EQUALS n) `the clauses of the fund excerpt`)

`the fund excerpt's references do not land` MEANS
        `fund clause subject of` 3  EQUALS LIST "the hours the fund holds"
    AND `fund clause subject of` 10 EQUALS LIST "the application form"
    AND `fund clause subject of` 7  EQUALS LIST "half-pay leave on the Treasury's account"
#ASSERT `the fund excerpt's references do not land`

§§ `1.25.3.1(11)-(14)`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p97 Heading of clause 11 ("miscellaneous provisions").

-- Clause 11ב and clause 13: paid sick leave counts as work for seniority, for
-- sick-day accrual and as service for every purpose — except, by clause 13's
-- note, that no sick days accrue while sick days are used before retiring.
-- Clause 11ג: unpaid leave suspends the employment relation, so no sick days
-- accrue in it.
DECLARE `kind of period` IS ONE OF
    `a period of paid sick leave`
    `a period of paid sick leave used before retiring`
    `a period of unpaid leave`
    `a period of work`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p99 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p100 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p106 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p107
GIVEN k IS A `kind of period`, p IS A `purpose a period counts for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the period counts for` k p IF
    CONSIDER k
    WHEN `a period of work` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a period of paid sick leave` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a period of paid sick leave used before retiring` THEN NOT p EQUALS `sick-day accrual`
    WHEN `a period of unpaid leave` THEN FALSE

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p101 Heading of clause 12 ("illness in a sabbatical year").

-- Clause 12: on a study-fund sabbatical (unpaid leave from the employer), an
-- employee whom a doctor keeps in bed for more than two months and who cannot
-- go on studying reports to the study fund and to the owner; the fund stops
-- the monthly grant, and the owner pays salary by the position held on
-- leaving, charged to the accumulated sick days.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p102
GIVEN `months in bed on a doctor's advice` IS A NUMBER, `cannot continue the studies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `illness ends the sabbatical studies` `months in bed on a doctor's advice` `cannot continue the studies` IF
    `months in bed on a doctor's advice` GREATER THAN 2 AND `cannot continue the studies`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p103 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p104
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sick-leave action`
DECIDE `reporting illness in a sabbatical` IS
        (PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `report the illness to the study fund, with medical certificates`
         WITHIN 30)
    RAND
        (PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `report the illness to the owner the sabbatical was taken from`
         WITHIN 30
         HENCE (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
                MUST  `pay salary charged to accumulated sick days` amount
                WITHIN 30))

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p104
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.25 party` `sick-leave action`
DECIDE `the study fund stops the grant` IS
    PARTY `the study fund`
    MUST  `stop the monthly study grant`
    WITHIN 30

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p105 Heading of clause 13 ("sick leave as a period of work").
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p108 Heading of clause 14 ("carrying sick days over").

-- Clause 14: an employee first uses all the current employer's sick leave,
-- then asks earlier employers to certify the unused days. F-1.25-g: "ג. או
-- שהמורה יצא לחופשה ללא שכר כדין" is read as an exception to ב (a break in
-- service that was lawful unpaid leave is no break), as clause 8א(2) of
-- section 1.25.3.2 words the same condition; not as a third, alternative route.
@desc An earlier employer's certification of unused sick days, as clause 14 tests it.
DECLARE `earlier employer` HAS
    `paid severance to the teacher`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `breaks in the teaching service`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `every break was lawful unpaid leave` IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p109 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p110 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p111 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p112
GIVEN e IS AN `earlier employer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the earlier employer certifies the unused days` e IF
        NOT e's `paid severance to the teacher`
    AND ((NOT e's `breaks in the teaching service`) OR e's `every break was lawful unpaid leave`)

-- The other reading: (א and ב) or ג — lawful unpaid leave alone would do.
GIVEN e IS AN `earlier employer`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `certified on the alternative reading` e IF
       ((NOT e's `paid severance to the teacher`) AND NOT e's `breaks in the teaching service`)
    OR e's `every break was lawful unpaid leave`

`a teacher paid severance, whose breaks were lawful unpaid leave` MEANS
    `earlier employer` TRUE TRUE TRUE
`the two readings of clause 14 differ` MEANS
    `certified on the alternative reading` `a teacher paid severance, whose breaks were lawful unpaid leave`
    AND NOT `the earlier employer certifies the unused days` `a teacher paid severance, whose breaks were lawful unpaid leave`
#ASSERT `the two readings of clause 14 differ`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p109 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p112
GIVEN `used all the current employer's sick leave` IS A BOOLEAN, e IS AN `earlier employer`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sick-leave action`
DECIDE `carrying sick days from an earlier employer` `used all the current employer's sick leave` e IS
    IF `used all the current employer's sick leave` AND `the earlier employer certifies the unused days` e
    THEN    (PARTY `the employer`
             MUST  `pay salary for the certified unused sick days`
             WITHIN 30)
         RAND
            (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
             MUST  `reimburse the current employer`
             WITHIN 90
             LEST  BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 1.25.3.1(14): the earlier employer reimburses the current one at the teacher's total salary for sick days, social additions included")
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p113 Pointer to the binding form in section 1.25.3.6, whose text the corpus does not carry.

-- The clarification: payment for carried days is based on the last salary
-- before the sick leave, with the collectively agreed components and social
-- rights — "where the employee's role has not changed". F-1.25-h: where it
-- has, the text gives no basis; the basis is then an input.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p114
GIVEN `the role changed` IS A BOOLEAN, `last salary before the sick leave, with agreed components and social rights` IS A NUMBER, `basis set elsewhere when the role changed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `monthly basis of carried sick days` `the role changed` `last salary before the sick leave, with agreed components and social rights` `basis set elsewhere when the role changed` IS
    IF `the role changed`
    THEN `basis set elsewhere when the role changed`
    ELSE `last salary before the sick leave, with agreed components and social rights`

GIVEN `the role changed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
DECIDE `the basis the clarification gives` `the role changed` IS
    IF `the role changed` THEN NOTHING ELSE JUST "the last salary before the sick leave"

`the clarification gives no basis when the role changed` MEANS isNothing (`the basis the clarification gives` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the clarification gives no basis when the role changed`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p115 Pointer to chapter 2.1.10 (sick leave of kindergarten teachers of ages 3-4 joining the civil service), encoded there.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_1/p116 Pointer to section 1.25.5 (sick leave in pregnancy), encoded below.

