-- Examples (placeholder figures).
`a 30-hour full year with 40 hours absent` MEANS `sick-hours year` 30 1 40
#ASSERT `sick-day hours of the year` `a 30-hour full year with 40 hours absent` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `sick days credited at the year's end` `a 30-hour full year with 40 hours absent` EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `the declared absences are within the declaration days` (LIST 2, 1)
#ASSERT NOT `the declared absences are within the declaration days` (LIST 1, 1, 1)

`a married teacher whose spouse works` MEANS
    `family circumstances` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE 3 FALSE 5 0
#ASSERT `days a year for a child's illness` 10 `a married teacher whose spouse works` EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `days left for a child's malignant illness` 10 `a married teacher whose spouse works` EQUALS 105
#ASSERT `days left for assisting a person with a disability` `a married teacher whose spouse works` EQUALS 33

`an application after 4 years, nothing earlier` MEANS
    `half-pay application` TRUE 4 TRUE NOTHING 0 3
#ASSERT `half-pay sick leave may be approved` `an application after 4 years, nothing earlier`
#ASSERT NOT `half-pay sick leave may be approved` (`half-pay application` TRUE 4 TRUE (JUST 12) 3 3)

#TRACE `carrying sick days from an earlier employer` TRUE (`earlier employer` FALSE TRUE TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay salary for the certified unused sick days` AT 10
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body` DOES `reimburse the current employer` AT 60

§§ `1.25.3.2 פיצוי בעבור חופשת מחלה בלתי מנוצלת לעובדי הוראה הפורשים לגמלאות`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p1 Amendment note ("this section was updated on 27.5.2002").

-- 1(1): the 3.11.1980 summary's terms on compensation for unused sick leave
-- apply to teaching employees who left the service on or after 1.4.1980; the
-- compensation is for the balance at retirement with the last employer,
-- above one full position too.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_1__subpara_1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_1__subpara_1/p2
GIVEN `date of leaving the service` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 1980 compensation arrangement applies` `date of leaving the service` IF
    `date of leaving the service` AT LEAST 19800401

DECLARE `compensation action` IS ONE OF
    `apply for the compensation`
    `pay the compensation` HAS `compensation paid` IS A NUMBER
    `notify the treasury of the compensation due`
    `certify the transferred sick days`
    `claim reimbursement from the teaching-manpower division`

-- 1(1)א-ב: whom the retiree applies to.
DECLARE `addressee of a compensation claim` IS ONE OF
    `the district's manpower officer`
    `the owner that last employed the employee`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_1__subpara_1__cls_a akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_1__subpara_1__cls_b
GIVEN `paid by the Ministry on the eve of retirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `addressee of a compensation claim`
DECIDE `where to apply for the compensation` `paid by the Ministry on the eve of retirement` IS
    IF `paid by the Ministry on the eve of retirement`
    THEN `the district's manpower officer`
    ELSE `the owner that last employed the employee`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_1__subpara_1__cls_b/p2 Pointer to paragraph 8 below (redemption of days from earlier owners), encoded there.

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_2 Lead-in ("compensation is given in these cases"); the cases are its sub-paragraphs.

@desc A retirement or death, as section 1.25.3.2 asks about it.
DECLARE `retirement case` HAS
    `how the service ended`            IS A `end of service`
    `age at retirement`                IS A NUMBER
    `years of permanent or temporary service` IS A NUMBER
    `left survivors`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of service with a right to sick leave` IS A NUMBER
    `sick days used in the whole service` IS A NUMBER @desc half-pay or other part-pay sick leave counted in proportion to the pay
    `position fraction at retirement`  IS A NUMBER @desc the actual extent of the position, above one included
    `monthly salary on the eve of retirement` IS A NUMBER @desc the combined salary and every addition counted for severance pay (section 1.28.2); an input
    `days accumulated while working as a pensioner` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `end of service` IS ONE OF
    `retirement on pension`
    `retirement on pension for ill health, disability or illness, on a medical committee's finding`
    death
    `another ending`

-- 2א, second paragraph: reaching 55 "by 31 December" and retiring on the
-- 1 September "near the 55th birthday" gives compensation; reaching it
-- "after 1 January" and retiring on the 1 September near the birthday does
-- not. F-1.25-i: the 1 September nearest a birthday between March and August
-- is the one AFTER it, when the employee is 55 and 2א's first paragraph pays.
-- The reading adopted: "the 1 September near the birthday" is the one that
-- opens the school year of the birthday, so the second sentence refuses only
-- a retiree of 54.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_2__subpara_a akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_2__subpara_a/p2
GIVEN r IS A `retirement case`, `reached 55 by 31 December of the school year of retirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a retirement that gives compensation` r `reached 55 by 31 December of the school year of retirement` IF
    CONSIDER r's `how the service ended`
    WHEN `retirement on pension` THEN
            r's `age at retirement` AT LEAST 55
         OR `reached 55 by 31 December of the school year of retirement`
    WHEN `retirement on pension for ill health, disability or illness, on a medical committee's finding` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- F-1.25-i's evidence: months from a birthday back to the 1 September before
-- it and on to the 1 September after it; for a birthday in month m (1-12).
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months back to the 1 September before` m IS
    IF m AT LEAST 9 THEN m MINUS 9 ELSE m PLUS 3

GIVEN m IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the nearest 1 September is after the birthday` m IF
    12 MINUS `months back to the 1 September before` m LESS THAN `months back to the 1 September before` m

`for a June birthday the nearest 1 September comes after it, at 55` MEANS
    `the nearest 1 September is after the birthday` 6
#ASSERT `for a June birthday the nearest 1 September comes after it, at 55`

-- The note: no compensation for sick days accumulated working as a pensioner.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_2__subpara_a/p3
GIVEN r IS A `retirement case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick days that count for compensation` r IS
    max 0 (`balance of sick-leave days` r MINUS r's `days accumulated while working as a pensioner`)

-- 3: the balance is 2½ days for every month of service carrying a right to
-- sick leave, less the sick leave used in the whole service.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_3
GIVEN r IS A `retirement case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `sick-leave days earned in the service` r IS
    2.5 TIMES r's `months of service with a right to sick leave`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_3
GIVEN r IS A `retirement case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `balance of sick-leave days` r IS
    max 0 (`sick-leave days earned in the service` r MINUS r's `sick days used in the whole service`)

GIVEN r IS A `retirement case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `share of sick leave used` r IS
    IF `sick-leave days earned in the service` r EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE r's `sick days used in the whole service` DIVIDED BY `sick-leave days earned in the service` r

-- 4א-ג: more than 65% used — nothing; 36% to 65% — 6 days' pay for every
-- 30 days of balance; under 36% — 8. The bands meet without gap or overlap.
-- F-1.25-j: "for every 30 days" is read as a rate (pro rata), not as whole
-- blocks of 30.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_4 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_4__subpara_a akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_4__subpara_b akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_4__subpara_c
GIVEN r IS A `retirement case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days' pay for every 30 days of balance` r IS
    BRANCH IF `share of sick leave used` r GREATER THAN 0.65 THEN 0
           IF `share of sick leave used` r AT LEAST 0.36 THEN 6
           OTHERWISE 8

GIVEN r IS A `retirement case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days' pay of compensation` r IS
    `days' pay for every 30 days of balance` r TIMES `sick days that count for compensation` r DIVIDED BY 30

GIVEN r IS A `retirement case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `days' pay on the other reading, whole blocks of 30` r IS
    `days' pay for every 30 days of balance` r TIMES TRUNC (`sick days that count for compensation` r DIVIDED BY 30) 0

-- 6: a day's pay is 1/25 of the monthly salary on the eve of retirement.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_6 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_6/p2 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_6/p3
GIVEN r IS A `retirement case`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `a day's pay` r IS r's `monthly salary on the eve of retirement` DIVIDED BY 25

-- 2ב: on death after at least 3 years of permanent or temporary service,
-- leaving survivors, the compensation goes to the survivors alone, and only
-- if no more than 65% of the sick leave was used.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_2__subpara_b
GIVEN r IS A `retirement case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a death that gives compensation` r IF
        r's `how the service ended` EQUALS death
    AND r's `years of permanent or temporary service` AT LEAST 3
    AND r's `left survivors`
    AND `share of sick leave used` r AT MOST 0.65

-- 4 and 5: the compensation follows the actual extent of the position, above one included.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_5
@export Compensation for unused sick leave on retirement or death, under section 1.25.3.2 of the takanon
GIVEN r IS A `retirement case` @desc the retirement or death
      `reached 55 by 31 December of the school year of retirement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the employee reached 55 by 31 December of the school year in which they retired
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `compensation for unused sick leave` r `reached 55 by 31 December of the school year of retirement` IS
    IF `a retirement that gives compensation` r `reached 55 by 31 December of the school year of retirement` OR `a death that gives compensation` r
    THEN `days' pay of compensation` r TIMES `a day's pay` r TIMES r's `position fraction at retirement`
    ELSE 0

-- 7: in official education the treasury pays on a notice from the district's
-- teaching-manpower head; in non-official education the employee applies to the owner.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_7
GIVEN `official education` IS A BOOLEAN, `compensation due` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `compensation action`
DECIDE `paying the compensation` `official education` `compensation due` IS
    IF `official education`
    THEN PARTY `the district manager`
         MUST  `notify the treasury of the compensation due`
         WITHIN 30
         HENCE (PARTY `the employer`
                MUST  `pay the compensation` amount PROVIDED amount AT LEAST `compensation due`
                WITHIN 30)
    ELSE PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MAY   `apply for the compensation`
         HENCE (PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
                MUST  `pay the compensation` amount PROVIDED amount AT LEAST `compensation due`
                WITHIN 30)

-- 8 (from 31.8.98): sick days move from owner to owner for compensation, if
-- the teacher had no severance from that employer and no break in continuity
-- (approved leave aside), on the earlier owner's signed certificate of the
-- seven listed facts (form 1.25.3.8). The last owner pays, under the usual
-- criteria (age, death, share used); owners are reimbursed as before, on
-- detailed individual claims to the teaching-manpower division.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_a akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_a__cls_1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_a__cls_2
GIVEN `received severance from that employer` IS A BOOLEAN, `breaks in continuity other than approved leave` IS A BOOLEAN, `date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sick days may be carried to the next owner for compensation` `received severance from that employer` `breaks in continuity other than approved leave` `date` IF
    `date` AT LEAST 19980831
    AND NOT `received severance from that employer`
    AND NOT `breaks in continuity other than approved leave`

DECLARE `fact the transfer certificate states` IS ONE OF
    `the teacher's name and identity number`
    `the date of birth`
    `the period of work and the share of a position`
    `days or hours accumulated, in full-position terms`
    `days or hours used, in full-position terms`
    `the balance of sick days`
    `the employer's confirmation of no severance and no break in continuity`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_b akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_b__cls_2 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_b__cls_3 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_b__cls_4 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_b__cls_5 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_b__cls_6 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_b__cls_7
`the facts a transfer certificate must state` MEANS
    LIST `the teacher's name and identity number`,
         `the date of birth`,
         `the period of work and the share of a position`,
         `days or hours accumulated, in full-position terms`,
         `days or hours used, in full-position terms`,
         `the balance of sick days`,
         `the employer's confirmation of no severance and no break in continuity`

GIVEN stated IS A LIST OF `fact the transfer certificate states`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate is complete` stated IF
    all (GIVEN f YIELD elem f stated) `the facts a transfer certificate must state`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_b__cls_7/p2 Pointer to the certificate form in section 1.25.3.8, whose text the corpus does not carry.

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_c
`the owner that pays carried-over compensation` MEANS `the owner that last employed the employee`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2__para_8__subpara_d
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `compensation action`
DECIDE `claiming reimbursement for carried days` IS
    PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
    MAY   `claim reimbursement from the teaching-manpower division`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p2 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p3 Source list: a Director-General's circular and a joint committee's summary (first line).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p4 Source list: the joint committee's summary (continued).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p5 Source list: the joint committee's summary (continued).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p6 Source list: labour-court judgments and a division circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p7 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p8 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p9 Source list: a Treasury labour-agreements instruction.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p10 Source list: an amendment of the State Service (Pensions) Law.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p11 Source list: a supplement to the 1988-90 wage agreement.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p12 Source list: a teaching-manpower division circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_2/p13 Source list: collective agreements, a circular and wage-unit notices.

-- Examples (placeholder figures): 30 years of service earn 900 days; 300 used
-- is a third (under 36%), so 8 days' pay per 30 days of the 600 left.
`a retiree of 60 who used a third` MEANS
    `retirement case` `retirement on pension` 60 30 TRUE 360 300 1 25000 0
#ASSERT `balance of sick-leave days` `a retiree of 60 who used a third` EQUALS 600
#ASSERT `days' pay of compensation` `a retiree of 60 who used a third` EQUALS 160
#ASSERT `compensation for unused sick leave` `a retiree of 60 who used a third` FALSE EQUALS 160000

-- F-1.25-j's evidence: a balance of 45 days in the 36-65% band.
-- 40 months earn 100 days; 55 used (55%) leaves 45: 9 days' pay pro rata, 6 in whole blocks.
`for every 30 days: pro rata and whole blocks differ` MEANS
    NOT (`days' pay of compensation` (`retirement case` `retirement on pension` 60 30 TRUE 40 55 1 25000 0)
         EQUALS `days' pay on the other reading, whole blocks of 30` (`retirement case` `retirement on pension` 60 30 TRUE 40 55 1 25000 0))
#ASSERT `for every 30 days: pro rata and whole blocks differ`

-- A retiree of 54 who reached 55 after 1 January gets nothing; one who reached it by 31 December does.
#ASSERT `compensation for unused sick leave` (`retirement case` `retirement on pension` 54 30 TRUE 360 300 1 25000 0) FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `compensation for unused sick leave` (`retirement case` `retirement on pension` 54 30 TRUE 360 300 1 25000 0) TRUE EQUALS 160000

#TRACE `paying the compensation` TRUE 160000 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the district manager` DOES `notify the treasury of the compensation due` AT 5
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the compensation` 160000 AT 20

§§ `1.25.3.3–1.25.3.8 Forms`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_3/p1 Title of the declaration form for a child's illness; the form's text is not in the corpus.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_4/p1 Title of the declaration form for a parent's illness; the form's text is not in the corpus.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_5/p1 Title of the declaration form for a spouse's illness; the form's text is not in the corpus.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_6/p1 Title of the certificate form for carrying sick days from an earlier owner; the form's text is not in the corpus.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_7/p1 Title of the declaration form for a partner's pregnancy and birth; the form's text is not in the corpus.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_8/p1 Title of the certificate form for carrying sick days for redemption; the form's text is not in the corpus.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_3_8/p2 Navigation line of the source page ("more contents on the subject").

§§ `1.25.4 חופשת נישואין`

-- An employee who for whatever reason cannot set the wedding in the vacation
-- is entitled to 6 working days of leave, 2 paid and 4 unpaid. F-1.25-s: the
-- unpaid 4 are an entitlement here and a matter the district manager "may
-- approve" in section 1.25.7.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_4/p1
GIVEN `cannot set the wedding in the vacation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `paid marriage-leave days` `cannot set the wedding in the vacation` IS
    IF `cannot set the wedding in the vacation` THEN 2 ELSE 0

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_4/p1
GIVEN `cannot set the wedding in the vacation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `unpaid marriage-leave days` `cannot set the wedding in the vacation` IS
    IF `cannot set the wedding in the vacation` THEN 4 ELSE 0

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_4/p2 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_4/p3 Source list: a Director-General's circular.

§§ `1.25.5 חופשה לרגל היריון ולידה, אימוץ או הפלה`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p1 Sub-heading ("the period of pregnancy").

DECLARE `pregnancy action` IS ONE OF
    `notify the employer of the pregnancy`
    `report the pregnancy to the supervision and the district office`
    `give maternity leave`
    `employ her during maternity leave`
    `notify HR of her choice on hospitalisation`
    `notify the employer of the choice to split the leave`
    `notify the employer of the choice to extend the leave`
    `contribute to the pension fund for the maternity weeks`
    `let her return to work`
    `request additional unpaid leave`
    `decide on additional unpaid leave`

-- 1: in the fifth month of pregnancy the employee notifies the employer:
-- teachers and instructors through their principals, who report to the
-- supervision and the district office; kindergarten teachers directly to the
-- supervision and the district office (and the owner). Time in months of the
-- pregnancy, counted from its start.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p2 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p3
GIVEN `a kindergarten teacher` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `pregnancy action`
DECIDE `notice of a pregnancy` `a kindergarten teacher` IS
    IF `a kindergarten teacher`
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `report the pregnancy to the supervision and the district office`
         WITHIN 5
         LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.5(1): a kindergarten teacher reports the pregnancy in its fifth month"
    ELSE PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `notify the employer of the pregnancy`
         WITHIN 5
         HENCE (PARTY `the school principal`
                MUST  `report the pregnancy to the supervision and the district office`
                WITHIN 1)
         LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.5(1): the pregnancy is notified in its fifth month"

-- 2: absence in the months of pregnancy, or for IVF, as far as a doctor
-- confirms in writing it is needed, is a sick absence (sick leave may be used);
-- the certificate needs the district health office's approval.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p4 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p5
GIVEN `days the doctor confirmed in writing` IS A NUMBER, `the district health office approved the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `pregnancy days treated as sick leave` `days the doctor confirmed in writing` `the district health office approved the certificate` IS
    IF `the district health office approved the certificate` THEN `days the doctor confirmed in writing` ELSE 0

-- 3 (and section 1.25.7 12ב): absence in the six weeks before the birth, on a
-- medical certificate, is charged to maternity leave or sick leave as she
-- wishes, or, if she asks, treated as unpaid leave.
DECLARE `charge for absence before the birth` IS ONE OF
    `charged to maternity leave`
    `charged to sick leave`
    `treated as unpaid leave`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p6 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p26
GIVEN `weeks before the birth` IS A NUMBER, `has a medical certificate` IS A BOOLEAN, `her choice` IS A `charge for absence before the birth`
GIVETH A MAYBE `charge for absence before the birth`
DECIDE `how an absence before the birth is charged` `weeks before the birth` `has a medical certificate` `her choice` IS
    IF `weeks before the birth` AT MOST 6 AND `has a medical certificate`
    THEN JUST `her choice`
    ELSE NOTHING

-- 4: an absence in pregnancy for an illness not caused by it is sick leave.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p7
`an absence in pregnancy for an illness not caused by it is sick leave` MEANS TRUE

-- 5: absence without loss of pay for medical supervision and routine tests at
-- an approved mother-and-child station (or outside it on its referral), up to
-- 40 hours over the pregnancy for a woman working a full week of more than 4
-- hours a day, and 20 for one working a full week of up to 4 hours a day;
-- approved on a medical certificate, charged to no leave; beyond the quota it
-- is sick leave. F-1.25-p: the cap is given only for a woman working a FULL
-- week; for anyone else the text sets none, and none is invented here.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p8 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p9 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p10 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p11
GIVEN `works a full week` IS A BOOLEAN, `hours a day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `hours of paid absence for pregnancy check-ups` `works a full week` `hours a day` IS
    IF `works a full week`
    THEN IF `hours a day` GREATER THAN 4 THEN JUST 40 ELSE JUST 20
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p12
GIVEN `hours of check-ups` IS A NUMBER, `quota` IS A NUMBER, `on a medical certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `check-up hours charged to sick leave` `hours of check-ups` `quota` `on a medical certificate` IS
    IF `on a medical certificate` THEN max 0 (`hours of check-ups` MINUS `quota`) ELSE `hours of check-ups`

`the check-up cap for a woman who does not work a full week is not set` MEANS
    isNothing (`hours of paid absence for pregnancy check-ups` FALSE 5)
#ASSERT `the check-up cap for a woman who does not work a full week is not set`

-- 6: IVF treatment of an employee (man or woman), with the treating doctor's
-- written approval and notice in advance to the person in charge, is a sick absence.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p13
GIVEN `the treating doctor approved in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `gave notice in advance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an IVF absence is sick leave` `the treating doctor approved in writing` `gave notice in advance` IF
    `the treating doctor approved in writing` AND `gave notice in advance`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p14 Pointer to section 1.28.2 (limits on dismissing a pregnant employee), encoded there.

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p15 Sub-heading ("maternity leave").

-- 1: "birth" is the birth of a live child or a birth after 26 weeks of pregnancy.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p16
GIVEN `born alive` IS A BOOLEAN, `weeks of pregnancy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a birth` `born alive` `weeks of pregnancy` IF
    `born alive` OR `weeks of pregnancy` GREATER THAN 26

-- 1א: she is given maternity leave and not employed during it. Time in weeks.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p17
GIVEN `weeks of leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `pregnancy action`
DECIDE `maternity leave is given and kept` `weeks of leave` IS
        (PARTY `the employer`
         MUST  `give maternity leave`
         WITHIN 1
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 1.25.5 maternity 1(a): an employee about to give birth is given maternity leave")
    RAND
        (PARTY `the employer`
         SHANT `employ her during maternity leave`
         WITHIN `weeks of leave`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 1.25.5 maternity 1(a): she is not employed during maternity leave")

-- 1ב: 14 weeks, of which 7 or fewer (as she wishes) before the birth; 14
-- weeks also for adopting a child of up to ten; 3 more weeks for every
-- further child of one birth.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p18
`weeks of maternity leave` MEANS 14

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p18
`most weeks of maternity leave before the birth` MEANS 7

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p19
GIVEN `age of the adopted child` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks of leave on adoption` `age of the adopted child` IS
    IF `age of the adopted child` AT MOST 10 THEN `weeks of maternity leave` ELSE 0

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p20
GIVEN `children born in the birth` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks of maternity leave for the birth` `children born in the birth` IS
    `weeks of maternity leave` PLUS 3 TIMES max 0 (`children born in the birth` MINUS 1)

-- 2: hospitalised for more than two weeks during the leave, she may either
-- extend the leave to the end of the stay (by at most 4 weeks, the leave not
-- exceeding 16 weeks in all) or split it, not counting up to 4 weeks of the
-- stay. F-1.25-m: the 16-week ceiling is below the 17 weeks a mother of twins
-- already has; read as capping only the extension, never cutting the leave.
DECLARE `choice on hospitalisation` IS ONE OF
    `extend the leave to the end of the hospital stay`
    `split the leave`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p21 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p22 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p23
GIVEN `weeks in hospital` IS A NUMBER, `weeks of leave before it` IS A NUMBER, c IS A `choice on hospitalisation`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks of leave after a hospital stay` `weeks in hospital` `weeks of leave before it` c IS
    IF `weeks in hospital` LESS THAN 2 OR `weeks in hospital` EQUALS 2
    THEN `weeks of leave before it`
    ELSE CONSIDER c
         WHEN `extend the leave to the end of the hospital stay` THEN
              `weeks of leave before it` PLUS max 0 (min (min `weeks in hospital` 4) (16 MINUS `weeks of leave before it`))
         WHEN `split the leave` THEN
              `weeks of leave before it` PLUS min `weeks in hospital` 4

`the leave of a mother of twins already exceeds the 16-week ceiling` MEANS
    `weeks of maternity leave for the birth` 2 GREATER THAN 16
#ASSERT `the leave of a mother of twins already exceeds the 16-week ceiling`

-- She tells HR (or the person it empowers) of her choice; HR charges her sick
-- days and tells national insurance, through her.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p24
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `pregnancy action`
DECIDE `telling HR of the hospitalisation choice` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `notify HR of her choice on hospitalisation`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.5 maternity 2: she notifies her choice"

-- 3: when the newborn must stay in, or return to, hospital for more than two
-- weeks during the leave — if she chose to split, she tells the employer 4
-- days before she wants to return; if she chose to extend, 4 days before she
-- was due back, or as early as she can. Time in days before the return.
-- F-1.25-n: the paragraph regulates the notice for two choices it never
-- grants: §2's choices are for a mother hospitalised herself.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p25 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p26 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p27
GIVEN c IS A `choice on hospitalisation`, `days before the return` IS A NUMBER, `she could not notify in time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `pregnancy action`
DECIDE `notice of a choice when the newborn is hospitalised` c `days before the return` `she could not notify in time` IS
    CONSIDER c
    WHEN `split the leave` THEN
        PARTY `the teaching employee`
        MUST  `notify the employer of the choice to split the leave`
        WITHIN max 0 (`days before the return` MINUS 4)
    WHEN `extend the leave to the end of the hospital stay` THEN
        IF `she could not notify in time`
        THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
             MUST  `notify the employer of the choice to extend the leave`
             WITHIN `days before the return`
        ELSE PARTY `the teaching employee`
             MUST  `notify the employer of the choice to extend the leave`
             WITHIN max 0 (`days before the return` MINUS 4)

DECLARE `who is hospitalised` IS ONE OF
    `the mother`
    `the newborn`

GIVEN w IS A `who is hospitalised`
GIVETH A LIST OF `choice on hospitalisation`
DECIDE `the choices the text grants` w IS
    CONSIDER w
    WHEN `the mother` THEN LIST `extend the leave to the end of the hospital stay`, `split the leave`
    WHEN `the newborn` THEN EMPTY

`the newborn's hospitalisation has notice rules but no granted choice` MEANS
    null (`the choices the text grants` `the newborn`)
#ASSERT `the newborn's hospitalisation has notice rules but no granted choice`

-- 3ג: notwithstanding 1ב, the leave may be shortened, with her consent and a
-- doctor's written approval, if the child is not alive — keeping at least
-- 3 weeks after the birth.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p28
GIVEN `the child is alive` IS A BOOLEAN, `she consents and a doctor approved in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `fewest weeks of maternity leave` `the child is alive` `she consents and a doctor approved in writing` IS
    IF (NOT `the child is alive`) AND `she consents and a doctor approved in writing`
    THEN 3
    ELSE `weeks of maternity leave`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p31 Pointer to section 1.25.2 (summer pay after maternity leave), encoded above.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p32 Pointer to the chapter on teachers' studies (pregnancy and maternity in a study year), encoded there.

-- 8: the owner contributes to the pension fund for an employee insured there
-- also for "the 12 weeks" of maternity leave. F-1.25-k: the leave is 14 weeks
-- under 1ב and 12 in the law section 1.25.7 quotes; the contribution is read
-- as the clause states it, for 12 weeks.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p33
`weeks of maternity leave the pension contribution covers` MEANS 12

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p33
GIVEN `insured in a pension fund` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `pregnancy action`
DECIDE `pension contributions in maternity leave` `insured in a pension fund` IS
    IF `insured in a pension fund`
    THEN PARTY `the local authority or owning body`
         MUST  `contribute to the pension fund for the maternity weeks`
         WITHIN `weeks of maternity leave the pension contribution covers`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the local authority or owning body` BECAUSE "section 1.25.5 maternity 8: the pension contributions continue through maternity leave"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p34 Sub-heading ("extension of maternity leave").

-- 11: absence from the end of the leave up to six months after it, as far as a
-- doctor confirms her condition after the birth needs it.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p35
GIVEN `months the doctor confirmed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months of absence on a doctor's word after maternity leave` `months the doctor confirmed` IS
    min `months the doctor confirmed` 6

-- 12א: after at least 12 consecutive months with the same employer up to
-- the leave, she may stay away from the end of the leave for a quarter of
-- the months worked, not past 12 months from the birth; part of a month is
-- not counted. 12ב: it is unpaid leave and does not count for seniority.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p36 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p37
GIVEN `consecutive months worked before the leave` IS A NUMBER, `months from the birth to the end of the leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months of extension under paragraph 12` `consecutive months worked before the leave` `months from the birth to the end of the leave` IS
    IF `consecutive months worked before the leave` LESS THAN 12
    THEN 0
    ELSE min (TRUNC (`consecutive months worked before the leave` DIVIDED BY 4) 0)
             (max 0 (12 MINUS `months from the birth to the end of the leave`))

-- 12ג: if she reports back, or says she wants to, before the extension ends,
-- the employer may not put off her return by more than 4 weeks. Time in weeks.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p38
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `pregnancy action`
DECIDE `no long delay of an early return` IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `let her return to work`
    WITHIN 4
    LEST  BREACH BY `the employer` BECAUSE "section 1.25.5 maternity 12(c): her return may not be put off more than 4 weeks"

-- 13 (and section 1.25.7 12ג): unpaid leave from the end of maternity leave to
-- the end of that school year is hers as of right. A further request goes to
-- the district manager by the date the approval sets; the manager approves by
-- the Women's Work Law where it applies and at discretion where it does not,
-- and says whether it is further maternity leave or ordinary unpaid leave —
-- further maternity leave only if she cannot return for health reasons tied to
-- the birth, on a certificate stating the expected period.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p39 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p27
GIVEN `months from the end of maternity leave to the end of the school year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months of unpaid leave after maternity leave as of right` `months from the end of maternity leave to the end of the school year` IS
    `months from the end of maternity leave to the end of the school year`

DECLARE `kind of further unpaid leave` IS ONE OF
    `further maternity leave`
    `ordinary unpaid leave`
    `refused`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p40 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p28
GIVEN `the Women's Work Law gives it` IS A BOOLEAN, `the law applies to her` IS A BOOLEAN, `the district manager's discretion` IS A BOOLEAN, `cannot return for health reasons tied to the birth, on a certificate with the period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `kind of further unpaid leave`
DECIDE `the district manager's answer to further leave` `the Women's Work Law gives it` `the law applies to her` `the district manager's discretion` `cannot return for health reasons tied to the birth, on a certificate with the period` IS
    IF (`the law applies to her` AND `the Women's Work Law gives it`) OR ((NOT `the law applies to her`) AND `the district manager's discretion`)
    THEN IF `cannot return for health reasons tied to the birth, on a certificate with the period`
         THEN `further maternity leave`
         ELSE `ordinary unpaid leave`
    ELSE `refused`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p41 Pointer to section 1.25.7 (the procedure for approving unpaid leave), encoded below.

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p42 Sub-heading ("adoption leave").

-- Adoption: §§1 and 12 apply, with the necessary changes, to an employee
-- receiving a child of up to ten for adoption; the leave "in section
-- (hereinafter 'the main leave')" runs from her notice to the welfare officer
-- (Adoption of Children Law, section 6), and "the absence in section 17" from
-- the end of the main leave. F-1.25-o: the first reference carries no number
-- and the second points at section 17, the labour court's ruling on returning
-- teachers. Read as §1's leave and §12's extension.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p43
GIVEN `age of the adopted child` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks of main leave on adoption, from the notice to the welfare officer` `age of the adopted child` IS
    `weeks of leave on adoption` `age of the adopted child`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `what paragraph n of section 1.25.5 is about` n IS
    BRANCH IF n EQUALS 1  THEN "maternity leave"
           IF n EQUALS 12 THEN "absence after maternity leave"
           IF n EQUALS 17 THEN "the labour court's ruling on a teacher returning from maternity leave"
           OTHERWISE "another matter"

`the adoption clause's "section 17" is the court ruling` MEANS
    `what paragraph n of section 1.25.5 is about` 17 EQUALS "the labour court's ruling on a teacher returning from maternity leave"
#ASSERT `the adoption clause's "section 17" is the court ruling`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p44 Heading of paragraph 15 ("the right to be absent from work").

-- 15(א): from the end of maternity leave to four months after it, an hour a
-- day, if she works a full position, on top of the Hours of Work and Rest
-- Law's breaks, without loss of pay. 15(ב), official education: a mother of a
-- live-born child, until the child is one, an hour on every day she works at
-- least six consecutive hours (the hour of (א) included), full or part-time,
-- in one or two parts, charged to neither leave nor salary. An hour is 60 minutes.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p45 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p46 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p47 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p48 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p49
GIVEN `months since the end of maternity leave` IS A NUMBER, `age of the child in months` IS A NUMBER, `works a full position` IS A BOOLEAN, `consecutive hours that day` IS A NUMBER, `in official education` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `paid minutes of absence that day for a mother` `months since the end of maternity leave` `age of the child in months` `works a full position` `consecutive hours that day` `in official education` IS
    IF    (`works a full position` AND `months since the end of maternity leave` LESS THAN 4)
       OR (`in official education` AND `age of the child in months` LESS THAN 12 AND `consecutive hours that day` AT LEAST 6)
    THEN 60
    ELSE 0

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p50 Heading of paragraph 15(ג) ("absence on a miscarriage").

-- 15(ג): after a miscarriage she may be absent, and for as long as a doctor
-- sets (at most six weeks) where her health needs longer; it is a sick
-- absence. The paragraph does not say how long without the doctor; section
-- 1.25.7 16ו quotes the law's one week, which is used.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p51 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p62 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p63 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p64
GIVEN `weeks the doctor set` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `weeks of absence after a miscarriage` `weeks the doctor set` IS
    max 1 (min `weeks the doctor set` 6)

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p52 Pointer to section 1.28.2 (resigning to care for a child, and severance pay), encoded there.

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p53 Heading of paragraph 17 (the labour court's ruling on a teacher returning from maternity leave).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p54 Lead-in to the ruling of 4 September 1980; its holdings follow.

-- 17א-ג: employment after maternity leave starts with the Ministry's notice of
-- the school; the employer may place her in another school of its choosing;
-- a teacher who refuses to teach except in a school of her own choice is not
-- placed, and is not paid for the time she does not work.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p55 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p56 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p57
GIVEN `refused the school offered` IS A BOOLEAN, `refused only to teach elsewhere than a school of her choice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid for the time not worked after maternity leave` `refused the school offered` `refused only to teach elsewhere than a school of her choice` IF
    NOT (`refused the school offered` AND `refused only to teach elsewhere than a school of her choice`)

-- F-1.25-k: the length of maternity leave, as section 1.25.5 states it and as
-- section 1.25.7 16ה quotes the law.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p57 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p58 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p59 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p60
`weeks of maternity leave as section 1.25.7 quotes the law` MEANS 12

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p59
`weeks before the birth as section 1.25.7 quotes the law` MEANS 6

`the section gives maternity leave two lengths` MEANS
    NOT (`weeks of maternity leave` EQUALS `weeks of maternity leave as section 1.25.7 quotes the law`)
    AND `weeks of maternity leave the pension contribution covers` EQUALS `weeks of maternity leave as section 1.25.7 quotes the law`
#ASSERT `the section gives maternity leave two lengths`

-- F-1.25-l: the extension of 12א against the law as section 1.25.7 16ה
-- quotes it — 24 months worked, counted from the seventh week after the birth.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p61
GIVEN `consecutive months worked before the leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months of extension as section 1.25.7 quotes the law` `consecutive months worked before the leave` IS
    IF `consecutive months worked before the leave` LESS THAN 24
    THEN 0
    ELSE min (TRUNC (`consecutive months worked before the leave` DIVIDED BY 4) 0) 12

`the two statements of the extension differ for 18 months worked` MEANS
    NOT (`months of extension under paragraph 12` 18 3 EQUALS `months of extension as section 1.25.7 quotes the law` 18)
#ASSERT `the two statements of the extension differ for 18 months worked`

-- Examples (placeholders).
#ASSERT `weeks of maternity leave for the birth` 2 EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `weeks of leave after a hospital stay` 3 14 `extend the leave to the end of the hospital stay` EQUALS 16
#ASSERT `weeks of leave after a hospital stay` 3 17 `extend the leave to the end of the hospital stay` EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `months of extension under paragraph 12` 40 3 EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `hours of paid absence for pregnancy check-ups` TRUE 6 EQUALS JUST 40
#ASSERT `paid minutes of absence that day for a mother` 6 8 FALSE 6 TRUE EQUALS 60
#TRACE `maternity leave is given and kept` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `give maternity leave` AT 0
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `employ her during maternity leave` AT 5

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_5/p58 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
