§§ `1.25.6 נוהל אישור חופשה בשכר לעובדי הוראה בחינוך הרשמי`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p1 Heading of paragraph 1 ("general").

DECLARE `paid-leave action` IS ONE OF
    `approve paid leave in the middle of the school year`
    `submit a request for paid leave` HAS `days before the date asked` IS A NUMBER
    `give an opinion on the request`
    `forward the request with an opinion`
    `decide on the request`
    `inform the applicant and send copies`
    `ask the Ministry for salary while paid for the mission`
    `commit in writing to serve a year in the same institution`
    `attach an insurance policy for the whole period`
    `approve paid leave for a delegation to Poland or the like`

@desc A request for paid leave, as section 1.25.6 tests it.
DECLARE `paid-leave request` HAS
    `purpose of the paid leave`           IS A `purpose of paid leave`
    `days of paid leave asked`            IS A NUMBER
    `applicant is permanent in an official institution` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took paid or unpaid leave in the last two years of work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `applicant is a supervisor`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `days between the request and the date asked` IS A NUMBER
    `declared being paid for the mission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `insurance policy attached`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the middle of the school year`    IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `purpose of paid leave` IS ONE OF
    `a mission directly tied to the employee's role`
    `a delegation keeping Israel's ties with the diaspora`
    `national sport representation`
    `lecturing by official invitation at an international conference abroad`
    `passive participation in a conference`
    `escorting pupils to Poland, Czechia or the like`
    `a diaspora-ties project such as Partnership 2000`
    `an official delegation of the international-relations division`
    `an educational mission to a CIS country`
    `escorting a spouse sent on a mission`
    `studies abroad`
    `another purpose`

-- 1.1: as a principle, no paid leave in the middle of the school year; 1.2:
-- in exceptional cases (a mission tied to the role, a delegation keeping the
-- ties with the diaspora) requests are discussed if made at least a month
-- before the date asked. 1.3: at most 40 days. Time in days.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p2
GIVEN r IS A `paid-leave request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an exceptional case for mid-year paid leave` r IF
       r's `purpose of the paid leave` EQUALS `a mission directly tied to the employee's role`
    OR r's `purpose of the paid leave` EQUALS `a delegation keeping Israel's ties with the diaspora`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p3
GIVEN r IS A `paid-leave request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the request is discussed` r IF
    ((NOT r's `in the middle of the school year`) OR `an exceptional case for mid-year paid leave` r)
    AND r's `days between the request and the date asked` AT LEAST 30
    AND r's `insurance policy attached`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p4
`most days of paid leave` MEANS 40

-- 1.4: the paid-leave committee at the head office, chaired by the head of
-- the teaching-manpower division, alone decides paid leave of any length,
-- except under sub-paragraphs 3 and 5; pay is for one position at most. One
-- who declared being paid for the mission does not also ask the Ministry.
-- F-1.25-q: 5.3 makes its own requests "subject to 1 and 2" — the
-- committee's procedure — though 1.4 takes all of 5 from the committee. Read:
-- 5.3's own words govern its requests, which go to the committee.
DECLARE `body deciding paid leave` IS ONE OF
    `the paid-leave committee at the head office`
    `a district committee for sport representation`
    `the district manager, deciding alone`
    `the central studies committee`
    `no one`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p5
GIVEN p IS A `purpose of paid leave`
GIVETH A `body deciding paid leave`
DECIDE `who decides under paragraph 1.4` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `national sport representation` THEN `a district committee for sport representation`
    WHEN `escorting pupils to Poland, Czechia or the like` THEN `the district manager, deciding alone`
    WHEN `a diaspora-ties project such as Partnership 2000` THEN `the district manager, deciding alone`
    WHEN `an official delegation of the international-relations division` THEN `the district manager, deciding alone`
    OTHERWISE `the paid-leave committee at the head office`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p5 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p28 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p33 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p34
GIVEN p IS A `purpose of paid leave`
GIVETH A `body deciding paid leave`
DECIDE `who decides paid leave` p IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `an official delegation of the international-relations division` THEN `the paid-leave committee at the head office`
    WHEN `studies abroad` THEN `the central studies committee`
    WHEN `escorting a spouse sent on a mission` THEN `no one`
    WHEN `passive participation in a conference` THEN `no one`
    OTHERWISE `who decides under paragraph 1.4` p

`for a 5.3 delegation, 1.4 and 5.3 name different deciders` MEANS
    NOT (`who decides under paragraph 1.4` `an official delegation of the international-relations division`
         EQUALS `the paid-leave committee at the head office`)
#ASSERT `for a 5.3 delegation, 1.4 and 5.3 name different deciders`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p5
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `position fraction paid in paid leave` `position fraction` IS min `position fraction` 1

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p6
GIVEN r IS A `paid-leave request`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `paid-leave action`
DECIDE `no double pay for a paid mission` r IS
    IF r's `declared being paid for the mission`
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         SHANT `ask the Ministry for salary while paid for the mission`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.6(1.4): one paid for the mission does not ask the Ministry for salary too"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 1.5: only a permanent employee of an official institution who took no paid
-- or unpaid leave in the last two years of work may apply (the committee
-- weighs the length of service); 1.6: not a supervisor.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p7 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p8 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p9
GIVEN r IS A `paid-leave request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply to the paid-leave committee` r IF
        r's `applicant is permanent in an official institution`
    AND NOT r's `took paid or unpaid leave in the last two years of work`
    AND NOT r's `applicant is a supervisor`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p10 Heading of paragraph 2 ("the procedure for submitting the request").

-- 2.1-2.5: the request (of at most 40 days) goes to the district manager or
-- unit; the supervisor of the institution gives an opinion after consulting
-- the principal; the district manager adds an opinion and sends it to the
-- division; the committee decides and answers the district; the district
-- manager tells the applicant and copies the supervisor, the principal and
-- the district treasurer.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p11 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p12 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p13 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p15
GIVEN r IS A `paid-leave request`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `paid-leave action`
DECIDE `the paid-leave procedure` r IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `submit a request for paid leave` days
          PROVIDED days AT LEAST 30 AND r's `days of paid leave asked` AT MOST `most days of paid leave`
    HENCE (PARTY `the supervisor`
           MUST  `give an opinion on the request`
           WITHIN 7
           HENCE (PARTY `the district manager`
                  MUST  `forward the request with an opinion`
                  WITHIN 7))

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p14
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.25 party` `paid-leave action`
DECIDE `the committee decides` IS
    PARTY `the paid-leave committee`
    MUST  `decide on the request`
    WITHIN 14

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p15
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `paid-leave action`
DECIDE `the district manager informs the applicant` IS
    PARTY `the district manager`
    MUST  `inform the applicant and send copies`
    WITHIN 7

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p16 Heading of paragraph 3 ("national sport representation").

-- 3: district committees of the district manager (chair), a teaching-manpower
-- representative and a treasury representative decide requests for sport
-- representation. F-1.25-r: section 1.25.10 sets the same district committee
-- with a general supervisor in the treasury's place.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p17
`the sport committee's members under section 1.25.6` MEANS
    LIST "the district manager (chair)", "a teaching-manpower representative", "a treasury representative"

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p18 Heading of paragraph 4 ("international conferences").

-- 4: an employee officially invited to lecture at an international conference
-- abroad may apply, attaching the programme, the invitation and the subject;
-- passive participation is not discussed.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p19 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p20
GIVEN p IS A `purpose of paid leave`, `programme, invitation and subject attached` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a conference request is discussed` p `programme, invitation and subject attached` IF
    p EQUALS `lecturing by official invitation at an international conference abroad`
    AND `programme, invitation and subject attached`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p21 Heading of paragraph 5 ("various delegations").

-- 5.1: an employee chosen to escort pupils to Poland, Czechia and the like asks
-- the district manager, who approves if the trip is part of the curriculum, an
-- authorised official approved it, and the pupils are of the employee's own
-- school (unless the Society and Youth administration asked otherwise); youth-
-- centre staff included; the district's manpower head orders the payment.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p22 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p23 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p24
GIVEN `the trip is part of the curriculum` IS A BOOLEAN, `an authorised Ministry official approved the trip` IS A BOOLEAN, `escorts pupils of the own school or was asked by the Society and Youth administration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `paid-leave action`
DECIDE `paid leave for a pupils' delegation` `the trip is part of the curriculum` `an authorised Ministry official approved the trip` `escorts pupils of the own school or was asked by the Society and Youth administration` IS
    IF `the trip is part of the curriculum` AND `an authorised Ministry official approved the trip` AND `escorts pupils of the own school or was asked by the Society and Youth administration`
    THEN PARTY `the district manager`
         MUST  `approve paid leave for a delegation to Poland or the like`
         WITHIN 30
         LEST  BREACH BY `the district manager` BECAUSE "section 1.25.6(5.1): the conditions are met and the district manager approves"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- 5.2: a diaspora-ties project: part of the school's curriculum, at most 50
-- participants nationwide in 5759 (1998-99), at most 10 days' absence, each
-- request approved by the education system's liaison to the diaspora.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p25 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p26 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p27
GIVEN `part of the school's curriculum` IS A BOOLEAN, `days of absence` IS A NUMBER, `the diaspora liaison approved` IS A BOOLEAN, `participants nationwide in 5759` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a diaspora project's paid leave may be approved` `part of the school's curriculum` `days of absence` `the diaspora liaison approved` `participants nationwide in 5759` IF
        `part of the school's curriculum`
    AND `days of absence` AT MOST 10
    AND `the diaspora liaison approved`
    AND `participants nationwide in 5759` AT MOST 50

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p29 Heading of paragraph 6 ("missions in the CIS").

-- 6: one sent by the Ministry on a mission to a CIS country may apply, subject
-- to 1.2; one escorting a spouse sent on duty has no paid leave.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p30 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p31
GIVEN p IS A `purpose of paid leave`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may apply for paid leave for a mission` p IF
    p EQUALS `an educational mission to a CIS country`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p32 Heading of paragraph 7 ("paid leave for studies").

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p35 Heading of paragraph 8 ("duties and undertakings").

-- 8: paid leave of more than two weeks needs a written undertaking to serve at
-- least a year in the same institution on return; no request is discussed
-- without an insurance policy for the whole period.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p36
GIVEN `days of paid leave` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `paid-leave action`
DECIDE `the undertaking to stay a year` `days of paid leave` IS
    IF `days of paid leave` GREATER THAN 14
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `commit in writing to serve a year in the same institution`
         WITHIN 1
         LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.6(8): paid leave of more than two weeks needs the undertaking"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p37
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `paid-leave action`
DECIDE `the insurance policy` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `attach an insurance policy for the whole period`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.6(8): without the policy the request is not discussed"

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p38 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p39 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p40 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p41 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_6/p42 Source list: a Director-General's circular.

`a lecture request a month ahead` MEANS
    `paid-leave request` `lecturing by official invitation at an international conference abroad` 5 TRUE FALSE FALSE 35 FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `may apply to the paid-leave committee` `a lecture request a month ahead`
#ASSERT `the request is discussed` `a lecture request a month ahead`
#ASSERT `who decides paid leave` `studies abroad` EQUALS `the central studies committee`

§§ `1.25.7 חופשה ללא שכר`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p1 Sub-heading ("unpaid leave in official education").
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p2 Heading of paragraph 1 ("general").

DECLARE `unpaid-leave action` IS ONE OF
    `be absent for a trip abroad or a family or social event`
    `notify the wish to return`
    `report for work at the place offered`
    `deduct national-insurance contributions from the last salary`
    `pay national-insurance contributions for the time beyond two months`
    `request an exceptional absence in writing, with reasons`
    `answer the request before the date`
    `approve an absence retroactively`
    `report the permits to the director-general`
    `forward the request beyond the district manager's power`
    `notify the intention to take a year of unpaid leave`
    `request unpaid leave for the next school year`

-- 1: teachers of official kindergartens, elementary, junior-high and
-- post-primary schools are at their institutions every school day; no
-- absence for trips abroad or family and social events in Israel.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p3 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p4
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `unpaid-leave action`
DECIDE `no absence for trips or events` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    SHANT `be absent for a trip abroad or a family or social event`
    WITHIN 12
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.7(1): no absence for trips abroad or family and social events"

-- "§§2-14 apply only to permanent teaching employees."
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p5
GIVEN `is permanent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paragraphs 2 to 14 apply` `is permanent` IF `is permanent`

-- 2א: approval guarantees a return to an official institution of the same
-- kind — not the same role, institution or locality.
DECLARE `guarantee on return` IS ONE OF
    `an official institution of the same kind`
    `the same role`
    `the same institution`
    `the same locality`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p6
GIVEN g IS A `guarantee on return`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `approval of unpaid leave guarantees` g IF
    g EQUALS `an official institution of the same kind`

-- 2ב-ג: a permanent employee sent on a mission of the state or the Jewish
-- Agency for up to 3 years may demand the position be kept (up to one
-- position); the owner may dismiss the substitute, however long the
-- substitution, or move a substitute who was permanent when transferred.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p7
GIVEN `years of the mission` IS A NUMBER, `sent by the state or the Jewish Agency` IS A BOOLEAN, `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `share of a position kept on a mission` `years of the mission` `sent by the state or the Jewish Agency` `position fraction` IS
    IF `sent by the state or the Jewish Agency` AND `years of the mission` AT MOST 3
    THEN min `position fraction` 1
    ELSE 0

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p8
GIVEN `the substitute was permanent when transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may dismiss the mission substitute` `the substitute was permanent when transferred` IF
    NOT `the substitute was permanent when transferred`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p8
GIVEN `the substitute was permanent when transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner may move the mission substitute to another position` `the substitute was permanent when transferred` IF
    `the substitute was permanent when transferred`

-- 3, 4: returning to the role offered at the end keeps every right earned
-- before the leave; notice on the date the approval sets and reporting at once
-- are the condition. One who did not notify, or did not return, is treated as
-- having left and given up every right — as is one who asked for leave or an
-- extension and stayed away though refused. Rehired later, such an employee is
-- new for every purpose but the seniority increment, unless the Civil Service
-- Commissioner deemed the service continuous. F-1.25-t: paragraph 12י(3) gives
-- the employee who escorted a spouse and did not return "full severance".
DECLARE `outcome of the end of unpaid leave` IS ONE OF
    `keeps every earlier right`
    `left and gave up every right`
    `resigned with full severance`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p9 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p10 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p11 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p12
GIVEN `notified on the date in the approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `reported at once to the work offered` IS A BOOLEAN, `stayed away though the request was refused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `outcome of the end of unpaid leave`
DECIDE `outcome under paragraph 4` `notified on the date in the approval` `reported at once to the work offered` `stayed away though the request was refused` IS
    IF `notified on the date in the approval` AND `reported at once to the work offered` AND NOT `stayed away though the request was refused`
    THEN `keeps every earlier right`
    ELSE `left and gave up every right`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p12
GIVEN `the Commissioner deemed the service continuous` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a rehired leaver keeps earlier service` `the Commissioner deemed the service continuous` IF
    `the Commissioner deemed the service continuous`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p10
GIVEN `days before the date in the approval` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `unpaid-leave action`
DECIDE `notice of return from unpaid leave` `days before the date in the approval` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `notify the wish to return`
    WITHIN `days before the date in the approval`
    HENCE (PARTY `the teaching employee`
           MUST  `report for work at the place offered`
           WITHIN 1
           LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.7(4): not returning to the work offered is leaving it")
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.7(4): no notice of return by the date in the approval"

-- 5: during the leave no rights are held or earned (sick leave, maternity
-- leave, holiday leave, recuperation pay, reserve-duty pay; pension, severance,
-- leave) — but with the Commissioner's consent the employee may pay the
-- Treasury 18.5% of the salary forgone, to buy pension and severance rights
-- for the period, which then also counts for the seniority increment (from 15.6.92).
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p13 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p14 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p15
GIVEN `salary forgone` IS A NUMBER, `the Commissioner consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `payment to buy pension and severance rights for unpaid leave` `salary forgone` `the Commissioner consented` IS
    IF `the Commissioner consented` THEN 18.5% TIMES `salary forgone` ELSE 0

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p15
GIVEN `paid the 18.5%` IS A BOOLEAN, `date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bought unpaid leave counts for the seniority increment` `paid the 18.5%` `date` IF
    `paid the 18.5%` AND `date` AT LEAST 19920615

-- 6-9: the Ministry may make approval conditional on staying a minimum period
-- after; refuses where it judges the employee will not be returned or cannot
-- return, and as a rule where medical tests are not concluded; as a rule no
-- leave over 6 years, ending as a rule at the end of a school year; it need
-- not take the employee back early, but the district supervisor may.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p16 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p17 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p18 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p19 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p20
GIVEN `the Ministry judges the employee will not or cannot return` IS A BOOLEAN, `medical tests concluded` IS A BOOLEAN, `years asked in all` IS A NUMBER, `an exception is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unpaid leave may be approved` `the Ministry judges the employee will not or cannot return` `medical tests concluded` `years asked in all` `an exception is made` IF
        NOT `the Ministry judges the employee will not or cannot return`
    AND (`medical tests concluded` OR `an exception is made`)
    AND (`years asked in all` AT MOST 6 OR `an exception is made`)

-- 10-11: leave of more than a month and at most two whole consecutive months,
-- with no other work: national insurance is deducted from the last salary
-- before it (or the first after it); beyond two months the employee pays for
-- the time beyond them. Time in days.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p21 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p22
GIVEN `months of unpaid leave` IS A NUMBER, `works for another employer or is self-employed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `unpaid-leave action`
DECIDE `national insurance in unpaid leave` `months of unpaid leave` `works for another employer or is self-employed` IS
    IF `works for another employer or is self-employed` OR `months of unpaid leave` AT MOST 1
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE IF `months of unpaid leave` AT MOST 2
         THEN PARTY `the employer`
              MUST  `deduct national-insurance contributions from the last salary`
              WITHIN 30
         ELSE    (PARTY `the employer`
                  MUST  `deduct national-insurance contributions from the last salary`
                  WITHIN 30)
              RAND
                 (PARTY `the teaching employee`
                  MUST  `pay national-insurance contributions for the time beyond two months`
                  WITHIN 30)

-- 12: the district manager may approve (not retroactively) unpaid leave for a
-- certified employee with at least 2 years in an official institution, in
-- the listed cases and on their terms.
DECLARE `case of unpaid leave` IS ONE OF
    `marriage`
    `pregnancy, on a medical certificate`
    `after maternity leave, to the end of the school year`
    `after paid sick leave`
    `volunteering for military service declared partial`
    `work in a kindergarten turned unofficial`
    `teaching in a non-official institution`
    `studies or research`
    `a trip abroad for a recognised educational body`
    `joining a spouse sent abroad`
    `an educational-administrative role`
    `rest after long teaching`
    `preparing for examinations`
    `another reason`

@desc A request for unpaid leave in official education, as paragraphs 12 to 16 of section 1.25.7 test it.
DECLARE `unpaid-leave request` HAS
    `case of the request`                IS A `case of unpaid leave`
    `certified`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `years in an official institution`   IS A NUMBER
    `retroactive`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `ability shown`                      IS A `pedagogical ability`
    `committed to teach a year after`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `months asked`                       IS A NUMBER
    `prior service in months`            IS A NUMBER
    `years of unpaid leave already`      IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `pedagogical ability` IS ONE OF
    `below average`
    `average`
    `above average`

-- 12א, marriage: 4 days after the 2 paid days. F-1.25-s: section 1.25.4 gives
-- these days as of right, to every employee who cannot marry in the vacation.
-- The other cases' terms follow: ז and ח need ability above average (ח also
-- the undertaking to teach a year after), ט and יב at least average, יב one
-- school year only, י (1) the shorter of the prior service and 5 years.
-- F-1.25-u: י(1) speaks of a woman "joining her husband" under a heading
-- that covers either spouse; read as applying to both.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p23 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p24 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p25 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p29 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p30 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p31 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p33 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p34 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p35 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p36 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p37 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p44 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p45
GIVEN r IS AN `unpaid-leave request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the district manager may approve under paragraph 12` r IF
        r's `certified`
    AND r's `years in an official institution` AT LEAST 2
    AND NOT r's `retroactive`
    AND `the case's own terms are met` r

GIVEN r IS AN `unpaid-leave request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the case's own terms are met` r IF
    CONSIDER r's `case of the request`
    WHEN `marriage` THEN r's `months asked` AT MOST (4 DIVIDED BY 30)
    WHEN `teaching in a non-official institution` THEN r's `ability shown` EQUALS `above average`
    WHEN `studies or research` THEN r's `ability shown` EQUALS `above average` AND r's `committed to teach a year after`
    WHEN `a trip abroad for a recognised educational body` THEN NOT r's `ability shown` EQUALS `below average`
    WHEN `rest after long teaching` THEN (NOT r's `ability shown` EQUALS `below average`) AND r's `months asked` AT MOST 12
    WHEN `joining a spouse sent abroad` THEN r's `months asked` AT MOST min (r's `prior service in months`) 60
    WHEN `another reason` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `preparing for examinations` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- 12ד: unpaid leave after paid sick leave is at the district manager's
-- discretion; on medical grounds a medical committee supports, it is unpaid
-- sick leave — as is the leave of one who exhausted sick leave, unless a
-- medical committee ended the service; return after two months or more for
-- health needs the district health office's approval.
DECLARE `kind of leave after sick leave` IS ONE OF
    `unpaid sick leave`
    `ordinary unpaid leave`
    `service ended for health reasons`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p29
GIVEN `medical grounds supported by a medical committee` IS A BOOLEAN, `exhausted sick leave` IS A BOOLEAN, `a medical committee ended the service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `kind of leave after sick leave`
DECIDE `leave after paid sick leave` `medical grounds supported by a medical committee` `exhausted sick leave` `a medical committee ended the service` IS
    IF `a medical committee ended the service`
    THEN `service ended for health reasons`
    ELSE IF `medical grounds supported by a medical committee` OR `exhausted sick leave`
         THEN `unpaid sick leave`
         ELSE `ordinary unpaid leave`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p29
GIVEN `months away for health` IS A NUMBER, `the district health office approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may return after a health absence` `months away for health` `the district health office approved` IF
    `months away for health` LESS THAN 2 OR `the district health office approved`

-- 12ו note: turning an official kindergarten unofficial is closing it, so the
-- teacher must first be offered work in an official kindergarten elsewhere.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p32
GIVEN `offered an official kindergarten elsewhere first` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `unpaid leave for an unofficial kindergarten is in order` `offered an official kindergarten elsewhere first` IF
    `offered an official kindergarten elsewhere first`

-- 12ז: the district supervisor may approve PARTIAL unpaid leave for teaching
-- in a post-primary or higher institution.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p33
`partial unpaid leave is possible for teaching elsewhere` MEANS TRUE

-- 12י(2)-(6): the leave keeps a teaching place in the district (as a rule
-- near home, and where possible the same school). One who does not return
-- on time is treated as resigning, with full severance under the civil-
-- service regulations, and is put on a priority list; rehired without having
-- taken severance, she is as a rehired civil servant: the Commissioner may
-- count the earlier service (pensions law, section 10(4)) where the break was
-- at most 24 months and she asked within 12 months of returning, weighing the
-- break's circumstances and the Ministry's recommendation; the division sends
-- every such case to the Commissioner.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p38
`a spouse-leave keeps a teaching place in the district` MEANS TRUE

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p39 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p40
GIVEN `returned on time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `outcome of the end of unpaid leave`
DECIDE `outcome under paragraph 12j(3)` `returned on time` IS
    IF `returned on time` THEN `keeps every earlier right` ELSE `resigned with full severance`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p41 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p42 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p43
GIVEN `took severance` IS A BOOLEAN, `months of the break` IS A NUMBER, `months from return to the request` IS A NUMBER, `the Commissioner's decision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `earlier service is recognised on rehiring` `took severance` `months of the break` `months from return to the request` `the Commissioner's decision` IF
        NOT `took severance`
    AND `months of the break` AT MOST 24
    AND `months from return to the request` AT MOST 12
    AND `the Commissioner's decision`

`not returning from spouse-leave: paragraphs 4 and 12j(3) disagree` MEANS
    NOT (`outcome under paragraph 4` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `outcome under paragraph 12j(3)` FALSE)
#ASSERT `not returning from spouse-leave: paragraphs 4 and 12j(3) disagree`

-- F-1.25-u's evidence: the words of 12י(1) reach a woman joining her husband only.
DECLARE `who joins whom` IS ONE OF
    `a woman teacher joining her husband`
    `a man teacher joining his wife`

GIVEN w IS A `who joins whom`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the words of 12j(1) reach` w IF w EQUALS `a woman teacher joining her husband`

`12j(1)'s words leave out a man joining his wife` MEANS NOT `the words of 12j(1) reach` `a man teacher joining his wife`
#ASSERT `12j(1)'s words leave out a man joining his wife`

-- F-1.25-s's evidence: section 1.25.4 entitles any employee; paragraph 12
-- leaves it to discretion and to certified employees of 2 years.
`a newly certified teacher marrying in term` MEANS
    `unpaid-leave request` `marriage` TRUE 1 FALSE `average` FALSE 0.1 12 0
`marriage leave: an entitlement in 1.25.4, a discretion out of reach in 1.25.7` MEANS
    `unpaid marriage-leave days` TRUE EQUALS 4
    AND NOT `the district manager may approve under paragraph 12` `a newly certified teacher marrying in term`
#ASSERT `marriage leave: an entitlement in 1.25.4, a discretion out of reach in 1.25.7`

-- 12יב: "the district manager will in no case approve unpaid leave for a seventh year".
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p46
GIVEN r IS AN `unpaid-leave request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the district manager may not approve a seventh year` r IF
    r's `years of unpaid leave already` AT LEAST 6

-- 13(א): a teacher preparing for higher-education or Ministry examinations
-- may have unpaid leave of up to 6 days a year (see section 1.25.8).
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p47
`most unpaid days a year for examination preparation` MEANS 6

-- 14, 15, 18: requests beyond the district manager's power go to the
-- teaching-manpower division, which handles retroactive unpaid leave and
-- extensions beyond 6 years.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p48 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p49 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p50 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p51 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p67
GIVEN `retroactive` IS A BOOLEAN, `years in all` IS A NUMBER, `within the district manager's power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the division handles the request` `retroactive` `years in all` `within the district manager's power` IF
    `retroactive` OR `years in all` GREATER THAN 6 OR NOT `within the district manager's power`

-- 16: for an uncertified employee, or a certified one with less than 2 years
-- in an official institution, the district manager may approve a temporary
-- break in service (not retroactive) of at most one school year, in the cases
-- listed — partial military service, marriage (4 days after 2 paid), illness
-- after paid sick leave on an approved certificate, pregnancy and birth by
-- the Women's Work Law (quoted, and encoded with section 1.25.5), a
-- miscarriage — or at discretion, for up to 3 months, for other reasons.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p52 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p53 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p54 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p55 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p56 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p65
GIVEN r IS AN `unpaid-leave request`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the district manager may approve a temporary break under paragraph 16` r IF
        ((NOT r's `certified`) OR r's `years in an official institution` LESS THAN 2)
    AND NOT r's `retroactive`
    AND r's `months asked` AT MOST 12
    AND (   (r's `case of the request` EQUALS `another reason` AND r's `months asked` AT MOST 3)
         OR (r's `case of the request` EQUALS `marriage` AND r's `months asked` AT MOST (4 DIVIDED BY 30))
         OR r's `case of the request` EQUALS `volunteering for military service declared partial`
         OR r's `case of the request` EQUALS `after paid sick leave`
         OR r's `case of the request` EQUALS `pregnancy, on a medical certificate`
         OR r's `case of the request` EQUALS `after maternity leave, to the end of the school year`)

-- 17: an exceptional absence for a trip abroad for a first-degree relative's
-- mourning or celebration is asked in writing, with reasons, through the
-- principal and the direct supervisor to the district manager, who answers
-- before the date; no absence before a written permit or against a refusal;
-- permits are reported to the director-general; no retroactive approval; a
-- breach is a disciplinary offence. Time in days before the absence.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p66
GIVEN `days before the absence` IS A NUMBER, `a written permit was given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `unpaid-leave action`
DECIDE `an exceptional absence for a relative's event abroad` `days before the absence` `a written permit was given` IS
    IF `a written permit was given`
    THEN PARTY `the district manager`
         MUST  `report the permits to the director-general`
         WITHIN 30
    ELSE    (PARTY `the teaching employee`
             SHANT `be absent for a trip abroad or a family or social event`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.25.7(17): no absence before a written permit; a breach is a disciplinary offence")
         RAND
            (PARTY `the school principal`
             SHANT `approve an absence retroactively`
             LEST  BREACH BY `the school principal` BECAUSE "section 1.25.7(17): direct superiors do not approve an absence retroactively")

-- 19: an extension of unpaid leave or of a temporary break is asked of the
-- district manager, with documents showing it is needed.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p68
GIVEN `documents show the extension is needed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an extension request is complete` `documents show the extension is needed` IF `documents show the extension is needed`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p69 Sub-heading ("unpaid leave in post-primary education").

-- Post-primary 1-8: the teacher must hold a permanent licence or tenure at a
-- school worked in for at least 5 consecutive years; notifies by 15 April; the
-- leave is for one year (two for an educational mission abroad), longer only
-- with the owner's approval; for one of the listed purposes; within one
-- position, no overtime. F-1.25-v: notice of return is due by 15 April here
-- and by 31 March under the official-education procedure below.
DECLARE `post-primary purpose` IS ONE OF
    `approved studies or recognised professional advancement`
    `teaching in a post-secondary institution`
    `managing an institution under Ministry supervision`
    `work in educational administration`
    `instruction and supervision`
    `work in educational television`
    `a recognised national mission`
    `another purpose approved unanimously by the joint committee`
    `a purpose not approved`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p75 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p76 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p77 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p78 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p79 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p80 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p81 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p82 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p83
GIVEN p IS A `post-primary purpose`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a purpose post-primary unpaid leave may serve` p IF
    NOT p EQUALS `a purpose not approved`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p70 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p72 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p73 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p74 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p85
GIVEN `holds a permanent licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `years of tenure at the school` IS A NUMBER, `years asked` IS A NUMBER, `on an educational mission abroad` IS A BOOLEAN, `the owner approved more` IS A BOOLEAN, p IS A `post-primary purpose`, `share of a position` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `post-primary unpaid leave is in order` `holds a permanent licence` `years of tenure at the school` `years asked` `on an educational mission abroad` `the owner approved more` p `share of a position` IF
        (`holds a permanent licence` OR `years of tenure at the school` AT LEAST 5)
    AND (`years asked` AT MOST (IF `on an educational mission abroad` THEN 2 ELSE 1) OR `the owner approved more`)
    AND `a purpose post-primary unpaid leave may serve` p
    AND `share of a position` AT MOST 1

-- 3ב: after two years the owner may dismiss the mission teacher's substitute as if in a first trial year.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p73
`the owner may dismiss a two-year mission substitute as in a first trial year` MEANS TRUE

-- Notices in post-primary, by 15 April: of going on a year of unpaid leave,
-- and of returning — one who does not notify the return is treated as resigning.
-- Dates as MMDD within the year.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p71 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p91
`post-primary notice deadline (MMDD)` MEANS 415

-- 5: where the principal cannot grant the request (difficulty in the school's
-- work, or the purpose unjustified), a committee of the Ministry, the owner and
-- the teachers' organisations decides by majority.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p84
GIVEN `votes for` IS A NUMBER, `votes against` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee grants the disputed leave` `votes for` `votes against` IF
    `votes for` GREATER THAN `votes against`

-- 7: the leave keeps the right to return and the continuity of seniority, but
-- earns no social rights; the teacher sees to them. A year of unpaid leave
-- not through the study funds, in which the teacher buys pension rights in a
-- recognised accruing fund, counts as a year of seniority — on applying to the
-- district's teaching-manpower office with the last employer's approval of the
-- leave and the fund's confirmation (from 1.9.94).
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p86 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p87 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p88 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p89 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p90
GIVEN `through a study fund` IS A BOOLEAN, `bought pension rights in a recognised fund` IS A BOOLEAN, `employer's approval and fund's confirmation filed` IS A BOOLEAN, `date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unpaid year counts as a year of seniority` `through a study fund` `bought pension rights in a recognised fund` `employer's approval and fund's confirmation filed` `date` IF
        NOT `through a study fund`
    AND `bought pension rights in a recognised fund`
    AND `employer's approval and fund's confirmation filed`
    AND `date` AT LEAST 19940901

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p92 Lead-in of paragraph 9 (unpaid leave for those elected head or deputy head of a local authority).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p93 Pointer to chapter 1.39 of the takanon, encoded there.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p94 Pointer to chapter 1.17 (the residence supplement in buying pension rights during unpaid leave), encoded there.

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p95 Sub-heading ("procedure in official education").

-- Official-education procedure: requests for the next school year, with
-- reasons and documents, to the district office by 31 March (later ones only
-- for a reason the Ministry finds reasonable); none handled before the
-- medical tests are concluded; the first decision binds until an appeal is
-- answered; a study-fund sabbatical (5744) needs a request too; stopping work
-- without written approval is resigning; a return is notified by 31 March,
-- or the post is given up.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p96 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p97 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p98 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p99 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p100 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p101 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p102
GIVEN `date of the request (MMDD)` IS A NUMBER, `the reason for lateness is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN, `medical tests concluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an official-education request is discussed` `date of the request (MMDD)` `the reason for lateness is reasonable` `medical tests concluded` IF
        (`date of the request (MMDD)` AT MOST `official-education deadline (MMDD)` OR `the reason for lateness is reasonable`)
    AND `medical tests concluded`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p103 Sub-heading ("an employee returning from leave").

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p98 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p104
`official-education deadline (MMDD)` MEANS 331

GIVEN `date of the notice of return (MMDD)` IS A NUMBER, deadline IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the return is notified in time` `date of the notice of return (MMDD)` deadline IF
    `date of the notice of return (MMDD)` AT MOST deadline

-- F-1.25-v's evidence: a junior-high teacher who is a state employee (both
-- procedures name such schools) notifying the return on 5 April.
`notice on 5 April: in time in post-primary, late in official education` MEANS
    `the return is notified in time` 405 `post-primary notice deadline (MMDD)`
    AND NOT `the return is notified in time` 405 `official-education deadline (MMDD)`
#ASSERT `notice on 5 April: in time in post-primary, late in official education`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_7/p105 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
