-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_9/p6 Source list: a Director-General's circular.

#TRACE `asking to defer reserve duty` 30 FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `apply to the principal at once` AT 0
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `sign the undertaking to serve in the vacation` AT 1
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `forward the documents to the town officer` AT 10
    PARTY `the school principal` DOES `send a copy to the district office` AT 10

§§ `1.25.10 היעדרות במסגרת "ייצוג לאומי" באירועים ספורטיביים בין-לאומיים`

DECLARE `sport action` IS ONE OF
    `approve paid leave for national representation`
    `submit the request to the physical-education supervisor`
    `pass the request to the national physical-education supervisor`
    `pass the request to the district's teaching-manpower department`
    `decide and inform the teacher`
    `approve paid leave for a private stay abroad`

-- The policy (¶1): encourage athletes to represent Israel while avoiding, as
-- far as possible, the loss of teaching days; hence the rules that follow.
-- 1-2: paid leave IS approved for a state-employed teaching employee asked to
-- represent the state at international events as an athlete, coach or judge,
-- in a representation the physical-education supervision approved (the five
-- kinds listed), at most twice a year and 12 days in all.
DECLARE `kind of national representation` IS ONE OF
    `a team or athlete representing Israel in an official competition`
    `the coach of such a team or athlete`
    `a judge invited to an international competition`
    `a national team's training camp or preparatory competition`
    `representation at a committee, convention or congress`
    `regular training`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p3 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p4 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p5 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p6 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p7 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p8
GIVEN k IS A `kind of national representation`, `approved by the physical-education supervision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is national representation` k `approved by the physical-education supervision` IF
    `approved by the physical-education supervision` AND NOT k EQUALS `regular training`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p2 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p9
GIVEN `a state employee` IS A BOOLEAN, `a national representation` IS A BOOLEAN, `leaves already this year` IS A NUMBER, `days already this year` IS A NUMBER, `days asked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid leave for national representation is approved` `a state employee` `a national representation` `leaves already this year` `days already this year` `days asked` IF
        `a state employee`
    AND `a national representation`
    AND `leaves already this year` LESS THAN 2
    AND `days already this year` PLUS `days asked` AT MOST 12

-- 3: in a non-official institution, where the Ministry cannot approve, the
-- request goes to the school or its owner, to whom the Ministry may recommend this procedure.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p10
GIVEN `a state employee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A STRING
DECIDE `where a sport request goes` `a state employee` IS
    IF `a state employee` THEN "the physical-education supervisor" ELSE "the school's management or owner"

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p11 Sub-heading ("the procedure for submitting and approving the request").

-- The procedure: the form goes to the district physical-education supervisor
-- (in teacher-training institutions, the institution's head) at least 30 days
-- before the event, with the invitation or schedule; it reaches the national
-- supervisor at least 21 days before, and the district's teaching-manpower
-- department at least 15 days before; the district committee decides and the
-- department informs the teacher. Time in days before the event, counted
-- from the request at 30 days out.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p12 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p13 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p14 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p17
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sport action`
DECIDE `the sport request's path` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `submit the request to the physical-education supervisor`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE (PARTY `the supervisor`
           MUST  `pass the request to the national physical-education supervisor`
           WITHIN 9
           HENCE (PARTY `the supervisor`
                  MUST  `pass the request to the district's teaching-manpower department`
                  WITHIN 6))

-- 4: the district manager (in teacher-training institutions, the head of the
-- teacher-training division) appoints and chairs a district committee with
-- the district's head of teaching manpower and a general supervisor; its
-- decision is written on the form. F-1.25-r: section 1.25.6(3) puts a
-- treasury representative in the general supervisor's place.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p15 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p18
`the sport committee's members under section 1.25.10` MEANS
    LIST "the district manager (chair)", "a teaching-manpower representative", "a general supervisor"

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p15
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.25 party` `sport action`
DECIDE `the district committee decides` IS
    PARTY `a district committee`
    MUST  `decide and inform the teacher`
    WITHIN 15

`the two sport committees differ` MEANS
    NOT (`the sport committee's members under section 1.25.6` EQUALS `the sport committee's members under section 1.25.10`)
#ASSERT `the two sport committees differ`

-- 5: the request names the event's exact dates only; no paid leave for a private stay abroad.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p16
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `sport action`
DECIDE `no paid leave for a private stay` IS
    PARTY `the district manager`
    SHANT `approve paid leave for a private stay abroad`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the district manager` BECAUSE "section 1.25.10(5): paid leave covers the event's dates only"

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p19 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_10/p20 Source list: a Director-General's circular.

#ASSERT `paid leave for national representation is approved` TRUE (`is national representation` `a judge invited to an international competition` TRUE) 1 5 7
#ASSERT NOT `paid leave for national representation is approved` TRUE TRUE 1 8 7

§§ `1.25.11 היעדרות בגין עדות בבית-משפט או בבית-דין`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_11/p1 Lead-in naming the supreme parity committee's decision of 28 April 1981; the arrangement follows.

DECLARE `testimony action` IS ONE OF
    `claim idleness fees and expenses from the court`
    `deliver the court's confirmation to the employer`
    `ask to testify in work hours and make up the hours`
    `approve testimony in work hours`
    `reimburse travel expenses`

DECLARE `testimony summons` IS ONE OF
    `by the employer or a government ministry, on matters known through the role`
    `by another person or body, on matters known through the role`
    `on matters unrelated to the role`

DECLARE `status of a testimony absence` IS ONE OF
    `absence on duty`
    `absence paid against the court's fees`
    `unpaid leave`
    `work hours made up by substitution`

-- 1-3: called by the employer or a ministry about matters known through the
-- role, the absence is on duty and travel is reimbursed; called by others
-- about such matters (a representative role included), the employee claims
-- idleness fees and expenses from the court, which sends them to the employer;
-- otherwise the absence is unpaid leave and any fees are the employee's — or,
-- on request, the district manager or employer approves testifying in work
-- hours with the hours made up by substitution, where there is a public
-- interest and no other expert, the fees then going to the employer.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_11__para_1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_11__para_2 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_11__para_3__subpara_a akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_11__para_3__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_11__para_3__subpara_b__cls_2 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_11__para_3__subpara_b__cls_4
GIVEN s IS A `testimony summons`, `asked to make up the hours` IS A BOOLEAN, `public interest and no other expert` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `status of a testimony absence`
DECIDE `status of the testimony absence` s `asked to make up the hours` `public interest and no other expert` IS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `by the employer or a government ministry, on matters known through the role` THEN `absence on duty`
    WHEN `by another person or body, on matters known through the role` THEN `absence paid against the court's fees`
    WHEN `on matters unrelated to the role` THEN
        IF `asked to make up the hours` AND `public interest and no other expert`
        THEN `work hours made up by substitution`
        ELSE `unpaid leave`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_11__para_2 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_11__para_3__subpara_b__cls_3 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_11__para_3__subpara_b__cls_3/p2
GIVEN st IS A `status of a testimony absence`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `testimony action`
DECIDE `the court's fees` st IS
    IF st EQUALS `absence paid against the court's fees` OR st EQUALS `work hours made up by substitution`
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         MUST  `claim idleness fees and expenses from the court`
         WITHIN 1
         HENCE (PARTY `the teaching employee`
                MUST  `deliver the court's confirmation to the employer`
                WITHIN 30)
    ELSE IF st EQUALS `absence on duty`
         THEN PARTY `the employer`
              MUST  `reimburse travel expenses`
              WITHIN 30
         ELSE FULFILLED

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_11/p2 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_11/p3 Source list: a Director-General's circular.

#ASSERT `status of the testimony absence` `on matters unrelated to the role` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `unpaid leave`

§§ `1.25.12 היעדרות ביום הזיכרון לחללי מלחמות ישראל`

DECLARE `relation to the fallen` IS ONE OF
    spouse
    parent
    child
    sibling
    grandparent
    `other relation`

-- 1: one bereaved of a spouse, parent, child or sibling in Israel's wars may
-- be absent on Memorial Day (from the eve), reported as justified paid
-- absence. 2: a first-degree relative (parents, grandparents, spouse,
-- children, siblings) of a victim of hostile action may be absent on the
-- general Memorial Day, counted as a workday.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_12__para_1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_12__para_1/p2
GIVEN r IS A `relation to the fallen`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid absence on Memorial Day for the fallen of Israel's wars` r IF
    r EQUALS spouse OR r EQUALS parent OR r EQUALS child OR r EQUALS sibling

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_12__para_2
GIVEN r IS A `relation to the fallen`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid absence on Memorial Day for a victim of hostile action` r IF
    NOT r EQUALS `other relation`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_12/p1 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_12/p2 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_12/p3 Source list: a Civil Service Commission instruction.

#ASSERT `paid absence on Memorial Day for a victim of hostile action` grandparent
#ASSERT NOT `paid absence on Memorial Day for the fallen of Israel's wars` grandparent

§§ `1.25.14 ערך קיזוז שעת היעדרות`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_14/p1 Amendment note ("this section was updated on 1.4.03").

-- 1 (from 1.9.84, replacing every earlier arrangement): single hours of
-- unjustified absence or unpaid leave are deducted from the month's salary at
-- the value of an hour by grade and seniority, and the summer pay is reduced
-- by the year's share of unjustified absence hours.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_14__para_1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_14__para_1__subpara_a akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_14__para_1__subpara_b/p2
GIVEN `hours absent` IS A NUMBER, `value of an hour by grade and seniority` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `deduction from the month's salary` `hours absent` `value of an hour by grade and seniority` IS
    `hours absent` TIMES `value of an hour by grade and seniority`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_14__para_1__subpara_b
GIVEN `summer pay` IS A NUMBER, `unjustified absence hours in the year` IS A NUMBER, `hours of the year's fixed work` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `summer pay after absences` `summer pay` `unjustified absence hours in the year` `hours of the year's fixed work` IS
    IF `hours of the year's fixed work` EQUALS 0
    THEN `summer pay`
    ELSE `summer pay` TIMES (1 MINUS `unjustified absence hours in the year` DIVIDED BY `hours of the year's fixed work`)

-- 2: a month's absence of LESS than 10% of the fixed work quota is deducted
-- from actual work hours only (not homeroom or matriculation-preparation
-- hours, nor the percentage additions for roles); one of MORE than 10% is
-- deducted proportionally from those too. F-1.25-x: exactly 10% is in
-- neither; read with the lighter rule, as no "more than 10%" is reached.
DECLARE `what an absence is deducted from` IS ONE OF
    `actual work hours only`
    `also homeroom and matriculation hours and role additions`
    `not stated`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_14__para_2__subpara_a akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_14__para_2__subpara_b
GIVEN `share of the month's quota absent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `what an absence is deducted from`
DECIDE `what the text deducts from` `share of the month's quota absent` IS
    BRANCH IF `share of the month's quota absent` LESS THAN 10% THEN `actual work hours only`
           IF `share of the month's quota absent` GREATER THAN 10% THEN `also homeroom and matriculation hours and role additions`
           OTHERWISE `not stated`

GIVEN `share of the month's quota absent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `what an absence is deducted from`
DECIDE `what an absence is deducted from, as read` `share of the month's quota absent` IS
    IF `share of the month's quota absent` GREATER THAN 10%
    THEN `also homeroom and matriculation hours and role additions`
    ELSE `actual work hours only`

`an absence of exactly 10% falls in neither band` MEANS
    `what the text deducts from` 0.1 EQUALS `not stated`
#ASSERT `an absence of exactly 10% falls in neither band`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_14/p2 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_14/p3 Source list: a Director-General's circular.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_14/p4 Source list: a supreme parity committee decision and a clarification.
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_14/p5 Source list: a Treasury wage-officer instruction.

#ASSERT `deduction from the month's salary` 3 120 EQUALS 360
#ASSERT `what an absence is deducted from, as read` 0.15 EQUALS `also homeroom and matriculation hours and role additions`

§§ `1.25.15 היעדרות לצורך השתתפות בועדת יועצים לבחירת מנהל בית ספר`

-- An employee absent to sit on an advisory committee choosing a state school's
-- principal has the interview hours counted as absence on duty, only on days
-- the employee would have taught; is entitled to the meal allowance of
-- civil-service regulation 26.222 and to travel costs under section 1.9.3 of
-- the takanon (inputs here); the committee's district coordinator confirms
-- the participation.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_15/p1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_15/p3
GIVEN `interview hours` IS A NUMBER, `a day the employee would have taught` IS A BOOLEAN, `the district coordinator confirmed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `hours of absence on duty for a selection committee` `interview hours` `a day the employee would have taught` `the district coordinator confirmed` IS
    IF `a day the employee would have taught` AND `the district coordinator confirmed`
    THEN `interview hours`
    ELSE 0

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_15/p2
GIVEN `meal allowance under regulation 26.222` IS A NUMBER, `travel costs under section 1.9.3` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `allowances for a selection-committee day` `meal allowance under regulation 26.222` `travel costs under section 1.9.3` IS
    `meal allowance under regulation 26.222` PLUS `travel costs under section 1.9.3`

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_15/p4 Heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_25__ssec_1_25_15/p5 Source list: a civil-service regulation.

#ASSERT `hours of absence on duty for a selection committee` 3 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0
